window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b095-d05e6d8547702a50.json"]={sha256:"d05e6d8547702a50f0c7520bd30750dd71c62f5b72419723a2515efc8a34c411",value:{"id":"b095","title":"清水混凝土模板與澆置","titleEn":"Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"清水混凝土的表面就是建築完成面，不能事後粉刷遮蓋，因此模板分割、繫桿孔排列、面板材料、脫模劑、配比與骨材一致性、澆置速度與振搗、樣板牆與驗收距離都必須在施工前定案。本課以安藤忠雄的光之教會與路易斯．康的沙克研究所為例，並以 ACI 347.3R 的成形面等級 CSC1 至 CSC4 與 ACI 301 第 6 節建築混凝土為框架，說明清水混凝土從設計意圖到長期維護的工程判斷。","summaryEn":"In exposed architectural concrete the surface is the finished building face and cannot be covered later, so panel layout, tie-hole pattern, facing material, release agent, mix and aggregate consistency, placing rate and vibration, mock-ups and viewing distance must all be settled before casting. Using Tadao Ando's Church of the Light and Louis Kahn's Salk Institute, framed by the ACI 347.3R formed-surface categories CSC1 to CSC4 and ACI 301 Section 6 Architectural Concrete, the course explains engineering judgement from design intent to long-term maintenance.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-concrete-steel","subcategoryTitle":"混凝土與鋼構施工技術","subcategoryTitleEn":"Concrete and steel construction technology","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-concrete-steel","learningTags":["structures","st-concrete-steel","concrete"],"architectureFamily":"concrete","architectureNodes":[["清水面等級與設計意圖","Surface category and design intent"],["模板分割、面材與脫模劑","Panel layout, facing and release agent"],["配比與材料來源","Mix and material sources"],["澆置與振搗控制","Placing and vibration control"],["樣板牆與量測驗收","Mock-up and measured acceptance"],["表面保護與維護紀錄","Surface protection and maintenance records"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[0,2],[1,3],[2,3],[3,4],[0,4],[4,5]],"diagram":{"type":"concrete","labels":["清水面等級與設計意圖","模板分割、面材與脫模劑","配比與材料來源","澆置與振搗控制","樣板牆與量測驗收"],"labelsEn":["Surface category and design intent","Panel layout, facing and release agent","Mix and material sources","Placing and vibration control","Mock-up and measured acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"施工規劃練習：一道清水牆長 12 m、高 5.46 m、厚 0.3 m，要求 CSC4 級。模板以 0.91×1.82 m 面板分割，12/0.91 ≈ 13.2 片不是整數，改用 13 片、每片 12/13 ≈ 0.923 m 的訂製寬度，高度 3 片，共 39 片，每片 6 個繫桿孔共 234 個。面板 21 mm 合板，設計側壓 50 kPa，背楞間距 250 mm 時撓度 ≈ 0.47 mm（約 L/531），滿足 L/400。牆體體積 12×5.46×0.3 ≈ 19.7 m³，上升速度限制 1.5 m/h 時供料 5.4 m³/h，約 3.6 h 完成。驗收距離訂為 6 m，可分辨約 1.75 mm 的缺陷。若現場改以 15 m³/h 供料，上升速度變為約 4.17 m/h，整面牆約 1.3 h 澆完，側壓接近液壓 24×5.46 ≈ 131 kPa，為設計值的約 2.6 倍，面板撓度增為約 1.23 mm，超過 L/400 的 0.625 mm，牆面會出現可見波浪與漏漿痕。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際建築。","textEn":"Planning exercise: an exposed wall 12 m long, 5.46 m high and 0.3 m thick is specified to CSC4. With 0.91×1.82 m panels, 12/0.91 ≈ 13.2 is not a whole number, so 13 custom panels of 12/13 ≈ 0.923 m are used, three high, 39 panels in all with 6 tie holes each, 234 tie holes. With 21 mm plywood, a design pressure of 50 kPa and studs at 250 mm, deflection is about 0.47 mm (about L/531), meeting L/400. The wall holds 12×5.46×0.3 ≈ 19.7 m³; limiting the rate of rise to 1.5 m/h means 5.4 m³/h of supply and about 3.6 h to complete. Viewing distance is set at 6 m, where about 1.75 mm defects can be resolved. If the site switches to 15 m³/h, the rate of rise becomes about 4.17 m/h and the wall fills in about 1.3 h, pressure approaches hydrostatic 24×5.46 ≈ 131 kPa, about 2.6 times the design value, and facing deflection grows to about 1.23 mm, beyond the 0.625 mm L/400 limit, so visible waves and leak marks appear. Values are teaching assumptions, not any real building.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b095-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「清水混凝土的性能目標與等級」與「模板分割、拼縫與繫桿孔排列」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Performance targets and surface categories\" and \"Panel layout, joints and tie-hole pattern\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b095-v13-01","title":"清水混凝土的性能目標與等級：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Performance targets and surface categories: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「成形面等級」如何影響清水混凝土模板與澆置的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Formed-surface category” governs force, deformation or durability in “Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"清水混凝土的第一個工程問題是「要多好」。ACI 347.3R 把成形混凝土表面分為 CSC1 到 CSC4 四級：CSC1 用於地下室牆等不重視外觀的位置，CSC3 可用於一般商業建築外牆，CSC4 則用於紀念性或地標建築；每一級對模板面材、表面孔洞比例與顏色均勻度的要求不同。ACI 301 第 6 節建築混凝土只有在契約文件指定時才適用，所以設計者必須在圖說中明確寫出哪些面是清水面、要求哪一級，否則承包商只會按一般結構混凝土施作。等級越高，模板、配比、人力與樣板成本都越高。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「成形面等級」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The first engineering question for exposed concrete is how good it must be. ACI 347.3R divides formed concrete surfaces into four categories, CSC1 to CSC4: CSC1 for places such as basement walls where appearance matters little, CSC3 for ordinary commercial exteriors and CSC4 for monumental or landmark structures, each with different requirements for form facing, surface void ratio and colour uniformity. ACI 301 Section 6 Architectural Concrete applies only when the contract documents designate it, so the designer must state explicitly which faces are exposed and to what category, or the contractor will simply build ordinary structural concrete. Higher categories cost more in formwork, mix control, labour and mock-ups. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Formed-surface category” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：表面孔洞比例 = 孔洞總面積/檢查面積。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Surface void ratio = total void area/inspected area.","failure":"常見誤解：「清水混凝土就是不粉刷的普通混凝土，不需要特別的規格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Exposed concrete is just ordinary concrete left unpainted and needs no special specification.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「成形面等級」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Formed-surface category”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-01-k1","title":"清水混凝土的性能目標與等級","titleEn":"Performance targets and surface categories","text":"清水混凝土的第一個工程問題是「要多好」。ACI 347.3R 把成形混凝土表面分為 CSC1 到 CSC4 四級：CSC1 用於地下室牆等不重視外觀的位置，CSC3 可用於一般商業建築外牆，CSC4 則用於紀念性或地標建築；每一級對模板面材、表面孔洞比例與顏色均勻度的要求不同。","textEn":"The first engineering question for exposed concrete is how good it must be. ACI 347.3R divides formed concrete surfaces into four categories, CSC1 to CSC4: CSC1 for places such as basement walls where appearance matters little, CSC3 for ordinary commercial exteriors and CSC4 for monumental or landmark structures, each with different requirements for form facing, surface void ratio and colour uniformity.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：清水混凝土就是不粉刷的普通混凝土，不需要特別的規格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Exposed concrete is just ordinary concrete left unpainted and needs no special specification. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「清水混凝土的性能目標與等級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Performance targets and surface categories\" is correct?","options":["清水混凝土就是不粉刷的普通混凝土，不需要特別的規格。","清水混凝土的第一個工程問題是「要多好」。","模板拼縫與繫桿孔只是施工痕跡，交給工地自行安排即可。"],"optionsEn":["Exposed concrete is just ordinary concrete left unpainted and needs no special specification.","The first engineering question for exposed concrete is how good it must be.","Form joints and tie holes are just construction marks that the site can arrange as it likes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清水混凝土的第一個工程問題是「要多好」。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The first engineering question for exposed concrete is how good it must be. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b095-v13-02","title":"清水混凝土的性能目標與等級：定量估算","titleEn":"Performance targets and surface categories: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「成形面等級」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Formed-surface category” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：表面孔洞比例 = 孔洞總面積/檢查面積。在 0.5 m×0.5 m = 250,000 mm² 的檢查框內量到孔洞總面積 400 mm²，比例 = 400/250,000 = 0.16%；若規格要求 ≤ 0.3%（教學假設值）則合格，若同一框內有一個直徑 25 mm 的大孔（約 491 mm²）就會超出。數值為教學假設，實際限值依規範表格與契約。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Surface void ratio = total void area/inspected area. In a 0.5 m×0.5 m frame of 250,000 mm², a measured void area of 400 mm² gives 400/250,000 = 0.16%; against an assumed limit of 0.3% it passes, but a single 25 mm diameter bughole of about 491 mm² in the same frame would exceed it. Values are teaching assumptions; actual limits come from the code tables and the contract. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在設計圖說中以立面圖標示每一個清水面的等級與觀看條件，並在施工前由業主、建築師與承包商共同確認；驗收時以固定尺寸的檢查框隨機抽取位置，量測孔洞比例並與規定值及樣板牆比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark each exposed face's category and viewing conditions on elevations in the design documents and confirm them jointly with owner, architect and contractor before work starts; at acceptance place a fixed-size inspection frame at random locations, measure the void ratio and compare it with the specified value and the mock-up.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"表面孔洞比例 = 孔洞總面積/檢查面積。在 0.5 m×0.5 m = 250,000 mm² 的檢查框內量到孔洞總面積 400 mm²，比例 = 400/250,000 = 0.16%；若規格要求 ≤ 0.3%（教學假設值）則合格，若同一框內有一個直徑 25 mm 的大孔（約 491 mm²）就會超出。數值為教學假設，實際限值依規範表格與契約。","textEn":"Surface void ratio = total void area/inspected area. In a 0.5 m×0.5 m frame of 250,000 mm², a measured void area of 400 mm² gives 400/250,000 = 0.16%; against an assumed limit of 0.3% it passes, but a single 25 mm diameter bughole of about 491 mm² in the same frame would exceed it. Values are teaching assumptions; actual limits come from the code tables and the contract.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「清水混凝土的性能目標與等級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Performance targets and surface categories\", which statement holds?","options":["只要強度等級相同，不同預拌廠的混凝土在外觀上沒有差別。","清水混凝土澆得越快越連續，表面就越均勻。","表面孔洞比例 = 孔洞總面積/檢查面積。"],"optionsEn":["If the strength grade is the same, concrete from different plants looks the same.","The faster and more continuously exposed concrete is placed, the more uniform the surface.","Surface void ratio = total void area/inspected area."],"answer":2,"explanation":"表面孔洞比例 = 孔洞總面積/檢查面積。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Surface void ratio = total void area/inspected area. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b095-v13-03","title":"清水混凝土的性能目標與等級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Performance targets and surface categories: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「成形面等級」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Formed-surface category” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在設計圖說中以立面圖標示每一個清水面的等級與觀看條件，並在施工前由業主、建築師與承包商共同確認；驗收時以固定尺寸的檢查框隨機抽取位置，量測孔洞比例並與規定值及樣板牆比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark each exposed face's category and viewing conditions on elevations in the design documents and confirm them jointly with owner, architect and contractor before work starts; at acceptance place a fixed-size inspection frame at random locations, measure the void ratio and compare it with the specified value and the mock-up. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在契約中引用 ACI 301 第 6 節或對應規範，逐面指定 ACI 347.3R 等級、孔洞比例、色差與平整度要求，以及樣板牆與觀看距離；這些要求要在投標前提供，讓承包商能正確估價。","observationEn":"Site practice: Cite ACI 301 Section 6 or an equivalent in the contract, specify ACI 347.3R category, void ratio, colour and flatness face by face, along with the mock-up and viewing distance, and issue these before tender so contractors can price correctly.","failure":"注意干擾：圖說只寫「清水混凝土」而未指定等級與驗收方法，完工後業主以地標級標準要求、承包商以一般結構標準施作，雙方對孔洞與色差爭執不下，最後只能大面積修補或塗裝，失去清水的意義。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Drawings that say only exposed concrete without a category or acceptance method lead the owner to expect landmark quality while the contractor builds to ordinary structural standards, and the two sides argue over voids and colour until extensive patching or painting defeats the purpose of exposed concrete. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在設計圖說中以立面圖標示每一個清水面的等級與觀看條件，並在施工前由業主、建築師與承包商共同確認；驗收時以固定尺寸的檢查框隨機抽取位置，量測孔洞比例並與規定值及樣板牆比較。","textEn":"Mark each exposed face's category and viewing conditions on elevations in the design documents and confirm them jointly with owner, architect and contractor before work starts; at acceptance place a fixed-size inspection frame at random locations, measure the void ratio and compare it with the specified value and the mock-up.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在契約中引用 ACI 301 第 6 節或對應規範，逐面指定 ACI 347.3R 等級、孔洞比例、色差與平整度要求，以及樣板牆與觀看距離；這些要求要在投標前提供，讓承包商能正確估價。","textEn":"Cite ACI 301 Section 6 or an equivalent in the contract, specify ACI 347.3R category, void ratio, colour and flatness face by face, along with the mock-up and viewing distance, and issue these before tender so contractors can price correctly.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「清水混凝土的性能目標與等級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Performance targets and surface categories\"?","options":["在設計圖說中以立面圖標示每一個清水面的等級與觀看條件，並在施工前由業主、建築師與承包商共同確認。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","清水混凝土的外觀好壞只能靠主觀感覺判斷，無法量測。"],"optionsEn":["Mark each exposed face's category and viewing conditions on elevations in the design documents and confirm them jointly with owner, architect and contractor before work starts.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The appearance of exposed concrete can only be judged subjectively and cannot be measured."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在設計圖說中以立面圖標示每一個清水面的等級與觀看條件，並在施工前由業主、建築師與承包商共同確認；驗收時以固定尺寸的檢查框隨機抽取位置，量測孔洞比例並與規定值及樣板牆比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark each exposed face's category and viewing conditions on elevations in the design documents and confirm them jointly with owner, architect and contractor before work starts; at acceptance place a fixed-size inspection frame at random locations, measure the void ratio and compare it with the specified value and the mock-up. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b095-v13-04","title":"清水混凝土的性能目標與等級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Performance targets and surface categories: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「成形面等級」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Formed-surface category” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"圖說只寫「清水混凝土」而未指定等級與驗收方法，完工後業主以地標級標準要求、承包商以一般結構標準施作，雙方對孔洞與色差爭執不下，最後只能大面積修補或塗裝，失去清水的意義。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Drawings that say only exposed concrete without a category or acceptance method lead the owner to expect landmark quality while the contractor builds to ordinary structural standards, and the two sides argue over voids and colour until extensive patching or painting defeats the purpose of exposed concrete. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：等級越高，模板、配比、人力與樣板成本都越高。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Higher categories cost more in formwork, mix control, labour and mock-ups.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「清水混凝土就是不粉刷的普通混凝土，不需要特別的規格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Exposed concrete is just ordinary concrete left unpainted and needs no special specification.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"圖說只寫「清水混凝土」而未指定等級與驗收方法，完工後業主以地標級標準要求、承包商以一般結構標準施作，雙方對孔洞與色差爭執不下，最後只能大面積修補或塗裝，失去清水的意義。","textEn":"Drawings that say only exposed concrete without a category or acceptance method lead the owner to expect landmark quality while the contractor builds to ordinary structural standards, and the two sides argue over voids and colour until extensive patching or painting defeats the purpose of exposed concrete.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「清水混凝土的性能目標與等級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Performance targets and surface categories\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","圖說只寫「清水混凝土」而未指定等級與驗收方法，完工後業主以地標級標準要求、承包商以一般結構標準施作，雙方對孔洞與色差爭執不下，最後只能大面積修補或塗裝，失去清水的意義。","模板拼縫與繫桿孔只是施工痕跡，交給工地自行安排即可。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Drawings that say only exposed concrete without a category or acceptance method lead the owner to expect landmark quality while the contractor builds to ordinary structural standards, and the two sides argue over voids and colour until extensive patching or painting defeats the purpose of exposed concrete.","Form joints and tie holes are just construction marks that the site can arrange as it likes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"圖說只寫「清水混凝土」而未指定等級與驗收方法，完工後業主以地標級標準要求、承包商以一般結構標準施作，雙方對孔洞與色差爭執不下，最後只能大面積修補或塗裝，失去清水的意義。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Drawings that say only exposed concrete without a category or acceptance method lead the owner to expect landmark quality while the contractor builds to ordinary structural standards, and the two sides argue over voids and colour until extensive patching or painting defeats the purpose of exposed concrete. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b095-v13-05","title":"模板分割、拼縫與繫桿孔排列：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Panel layout, joints and tie-hole pattern: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「模板分割與繫桿孔」如何影響清水混凝土模板與澆置的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Panel layout and tie holes” governs force, deformation or durability in “Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"在清水混凝土中，模板拼縫與繫桿孔不是缺陷，而是建築語彙：它們的位置、間距與對齊方式會永久留在表面上。安藤忠雄的作品常以約 910×1,820 mm 的模板與規則排列的繫桿孔構成立面節奏，路易斯．康在沙克研究所也讓模板接縫與繫桿孔成為表面的秩序。因此模板分割必須在建築設計階段與牆長、開口、樓層高度與轉角一起決定，並把繫桿孔放在面板上對稱的位置；若牆長不是面板寬度的整數倍，就會出現難看的窄條板。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「模板分割與繫桿孔」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In exposed concrete, form joints and tie holes are not defects but architectural vocabulary: their position, spacing and alignment stay on the surface permanently. Tadao Ando's work often uses forms of about 910×1,820 mm with regularly spaced tie holes to give elevations their rhythm, and Louis Kahn at the Salk Institute likewise let form joints and tie holes order the surface. Panel layout must therefore be settled at architectural design stage together with wall lengths, openings, storey heights and corners, with tie holes placed symmetrically on each panel; if a wall length is not a whole multiple of the panel width, an awkward narrow filler panel appears. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Panel layout and tie holes” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：牆長 17.5 m、面板寬 0.91 m 時需要 17.5/0.91 ≈ 19.2 片，不是整數。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 17.5 m wall with 0.91 m panels needs 17.5/0.91 ≈ 19.2 panels, not a whole number.","failure":"常見誤解：「模板拼縫與繫桿孔只是施工痕跡，交給工地自行安排即可。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Form joints and tie holes are just construction marks that the site can arrange as it likes.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「模板分割與繫桿孔」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Panel layout and tie holes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-05-k1","title":"模板分割、拼縫與繫桿孔排列","titleEn":"Panel layout, joints and tie-hole pattern","text":"在清水混凝土中，模板拼縫與繫桿孔不是缺陷，而是建築語彙：它們的位置、間距與對齊方式會永久留在表面上。安藤忠雄的作品常以約 910×1,820 mm 的模板與規則排列的繫桿孔構成立面節奏，路易斯．康在沙克研究所也讓模板接縫與繫桿孔成為表面的秩序。","textEn":"In exposed concrete, form joints and tie holes are not defects but architectural vocabulary: their position, spacing and alignment stay on the surface permanently. Tadao Ando's work often uses forms of about 910×1,820 mm with regularly spaced tie holes to give elevations their rhythm, and Louis Kahn at the Salk Institute likewise let form joints and tie holes order the surface.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模板拼縫與繫桿孔只是施工痕跡，交給工地自行安排即可。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Form joints and tie holes are just construction marks that the site can arrange as it likes. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模板分割、拼縫與繫桿孔排列」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Panel layout, joints and tie-hole pattern\" is correct?","options":["模板拼縫與繫桿孔只是施工痕跡，交給工地自行安排即可。","脫模劑塗得越多越好，可以保證拆模後表面光滑。","在清水混凝土中，模板拼縫與繫桿孔不是缺陷，而是建築語彙：它們的位置、間距與對齊方式會永久留在表面上。"],"optionsEn":["Form joints and tie holes are just construction marks that the site can arrange as it likes.","The more release agent the better; it guarantees a smooth surface after stripping.","In exposed concrete, form joints and tie holes are not defects but architectural vocabulary: their position, spacing and alignment stay on the surface permanently."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在清水混凝土中，模板拼縫與繫桿孔不是缺陷，而是建築語彙：它們的位置、間距與對齊方式會永久留在表面上。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In exposed concrete, form joints and tie holes are not defects but architectural vocabulary: their position, spacing and alignment stay on the surface permanently. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b095-v13-06","title":"模板分割、拼縫與繫桿孔排列：定量估算","titleEn":"Panel layout, joints and tie-hole pattern: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模板分割與繫桿孔」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Panel layout and tie holes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：牆長 17.5 m、面板寬 0.91 m 時需要 17.5/0.91 ≈ 19.2 片，不是整數。可選擇：改用 19 片、每片約 17.5/19 ≈ 0.921 m 的訂製寬度，或把牆長調為 19×0.91 = 17.29 m 或 20×0.91 = 18.2 m。牆高 3 片×1.82 m = 5.46 m，每片 6 個繫桿孔，19×3 = 57 片共 342 個繫桿孔。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 17.5 m wall with 0.91 m panels needs 17.5/0.91 ≈ 19.2 panels, not a whole number. Options: 19 custom panels of about 17.5/19 ≈ 0.921 m, or adjusting the wall to 19×0.91 = 17.29 m or 20×0.91 = 18.2 m. Three panels of 1.82 m make 5.46 m of height; with 6 tie holes per panel, 19×3 = 57 panels carry 342 tie holes. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以立面展開圖繪出每一道牆的面板分割、拼縫、繫桿孔與施工縫位置，並與開口、轉角、樓板邊緣對齊檢查；模板加工前由建築師簽認展開圖，現場組模後以捲尺與雷射抽查拼縫與繫桿孔位置。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Draw developed elevations of every wall showing panel layout, joints, tie holes and construction joints, checking alignment with openings, corners and slab edges; have the architect sign the developed elevations before forms are made, and spot-check joint and tie-hole positions on site with tape and laser after assembly.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"牆長 17.5 m、面板寬 0.91 m 時需要 17.5/0.91 ≈ 19.2 片，不是整數。可選擇：改用 19 片、每片約 17.5/19 ≈ 0.921 m 的訂製寬度，或把牆長調為 19×0.91 = 17.29 m 或 20×0.91 = 18.2 m。牆高 3 片×1.82 m = 5.46 m，每片 6 個繫桿孔，19×3 = 57 片共 342 個繫桿孔。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A 17.5 m wall with 0.91 m panels needs 17.5/0.91 ≈ 19.2 panels, not a whole number. Options: 19 custom panels of about 17.5/19 ≈ 0.921 m, or adjusting the wall to 19×0.91 = 17.29 m or 20×0.91 = 18.2 m. Three panels of 1.82 m make 5.46 m of height; with 6 tie holes per panel, 19×3 = 57 panels carry 342 tie holes. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模板分割、拼縫與繫桿孔排列」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Panel layout, joints and tie-hole pattern\", which statement holds?","options":["牆長 17.5 m、面板寬 0.91 m 時需要 17.5/0.91 ≈ 19.2 片，不是整數。","清水模板只要表面光滑就好，背楞間距照一般結構模板即可。","樣板牆只是給業主看的展示品，正式施工時不需要再參照。"],"optionsEn":["A 17.5 m wall with 0.91 m panels needs 17.5/0.91 ≈ 19.2 panels, not a whole number.","Exposed-concrete forms only need a smooth facing; stud spacing can follow ordinary structural forms.","The mock-up is just a showpiece for the owner and need not be referred to during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"牆長 17.5 m、面板寬 0.91 m 時需要 17.5/0.91 ≈ 19.2 片，不是整數。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 17.5 m wall with 0.91 m panels needs 17.5/0.91 ≈ 19.2 panels, not a whole number. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b095-v13-07","title":"模板分割、拼縫與繫桿孔排列：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Panel layout, joints and tie-hole pattern: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模板分割與繫桿孔」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Panel layout and tie holes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以立面展開圖繪出每一道牆的面板分割、拼縫、繫桿孔與施工縫位置，並與開口、轉角、樓板邊緣對齊檢查；模板加工前由建築師簽認展開圖，現場組模後以捲尺與雷射抽查拼縫與繫桿孔位置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Draw developed elevations of every wall showing panel layout, joints, tie holes and construction joints, checking alignment with openings, corners and slab edges; have the architect sign the developed elevations before forms are made, and spot-check joint and tie-hole positions on site with tape and laser after assembly. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把模板分割展開圖列為建築設計圖的一部分，施工縫、繫桿孔與拼縫的位置與構造詳圖（例如倒角、凹槽、繫桿錐形套）都要在開工前定案；任何現場調整須經建築師書面同意。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make the developed formwork elevations part of the architectural drawings, and settle construction joints, tie holes and joint details such as chamfers, reveals and tie cones before work starts; any site adjustment needs the architect's written approval.","failure":"注意干擾：模板分割在現場臨時決定，牆端出現 200 mm 的窄條板，繫桿孔在轉角兩側無法對齊，施工縫位置與拼縫錯開形成雜亂的水平線，整面清水牆的秩序被破壞且無法修正。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Deciding the layout on site leaves a 200 mm filler strip at the wall end, tie holes that cannot line up on either side of a corner, and construction joints offset from panel joints that form messy horizontal lines, destroying the order of the whole exposed wall beyond correction. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以立面展開圖繪出每一道牆的面板分割、拼縫、繫桿孔與施工縫位置，並與開口、轉角、樓板邊緣對齊檢查；模板加工前由建築師簽認展開圖，現場組模後以捲尺與雷射抽查拼縫與繫桿孔位置。","textEn":"Draw developed elevations of every wall showing panel layout, joints, tie holes and construction joints, checking alignment with openings, corners and slab edges; have the architect sign the developed elevations before forms are made, and spot-check joint and tie-hole positions on site with tape and laser after assembly.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把模板分割展開圖列為建築設計圖的一部分，施工縫、繫桿孔與拼縫的位置與構造詳圖（例如倒角、凹槽、繫桿錐形套）都要在開工前定案；任何現場調整須經建築師書面同意。","textEn":"Make the developed formwork elevations part of the architectural drawings, and settle construction joints, tie holes and joint details such as chamfers, reveals and tie cones before work starts; any site adjustment needs the architect's written approval.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模板分割、拼縫與繫桿孔排列」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Panel layout, joints and tie-hole pattern\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以立面展開圖繪出每一道牆的面板分割、拼縫、繫桿孔與施工縫位置，並與開口、轉角、樓板邊緣對齊檢查。","清水混凝土很耐久，不需要任何表面保護與修補計畫。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Draw developed elevations of every wall showing panel layout, joints, tie holes and construction joints, checking alignment with openings, corners and slab edges.","Exposed concrete is durable and needs no surface protection or repair plan."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以立面展開圖繪出每一道牆的面板分割、拼縫、繫桿孔與施工縫位置，並與開口、轉角、樓板邊緣對齊檢查；模板加工前由建築師簽認展開圖，現場組模後以捲尺與雷射抽查拼縫與繫桿孔位置。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Draw developed elevations of every wall showing panel layout, joints, tie holes and construction joints, checking alignment with openings, corners and slab edges; have the architect sign the developed elevations before forms are made, and spot-check joint and tie-hole positions on site with tape and laser after assembly. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b095-v13-08","title":"模板分割、拼縫與繫桿孔排列：失效診斷","titleEn":"Panel layout, joints and tie-hole pattern: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模板分割與繫桿孔」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Panel layout and tie holes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"模板分割在現場臨時決定，牆端出現 200 mm 的窄條板，繫桿孔在轉角兩側無法對齊，施工縫位置與拼縫錯開形成雜亂的水平線，整面清水牆的秩序被破壞且無法修正。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Deciding the layout on site leaves a 200 mm filler strip at the wall end, tie holes that cannot line up on either side of a corner, and construction joints offset from panel joints that form messy horizontal lines, destroying the order of the whole exposed wall beyond correction. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此模板分割必須在建築設計階段與牆長、開口、樓層高度與轉角一起決定，並把繫桿孔放在面板上對稱的位置；若牆長不是面板寬度的整數倍，就會出現難看的窄條板。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Panel layout must therefore be settled at architectural design stage together with wall lengths, openings, storey heights and corners, with tie holes placed symmetrically on each panel; if a wall length is not a whole multiple of the panel width, an awkward narrow filler panel appears.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模板拼縫與繫桿孔只是施工痕跡，交給工地自行安排即可。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Form joints and tie holes are just construction marks that the site can arrange as it likes.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"模板分割在現場臨時決定，牆端出現 200 mm 的窄條板，繫桿孔在轉角兩側無法對齊，施工縫位置與拼縫錯開形成雜亂的水平線，整面清水牆的秩序被破壞且無法修正。","textEn":"Deciding the layout on site leaves a 200 mm filler strip at the wall end, tie holes that cannot line up on either side of a corner, and construction joints offset from panel joints that form messy horizontal lines, destroying the order of the whole exposed wall beyond correction.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模板分割、拼縫與繫桿孔排列」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Panel layout, joints and tie-hole pattern\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","脫模劑塗得越多越好，可以保證拆模後表面光滑。","模板分割在現場臨時決定，牆端出現 200 mm 的窄條板，繫桿孔在轉角兩側無法對齊，施工縫位置與拼縫錯開形成雜亂的水平線，整面清水牆的秩序被破壞且無法修正。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The more release agent the better; it guarantees a smooth surface after stripping.","Deciding the layout on site leaves a 200 mm filler strip at the wall end, tie holes that cannot line up on either side of a corner, and construction joints offset from panel joints that form messy horizontal lines, destroying the order of the whole exposed wall beyond correction."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模板分割在現場臨時決定，牆端出現 200 mm 的窄條板，繫桿孔在轉角兩側無法對齊，施工縫位置與拼縫錯開形成雜亂的水平線，整面清水牆的秩序被破壞且無法修正。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Deciding the layout on site leaves a 200 mm filler strip at the wall end, tie holes that cannot line up on either side of a corner, and construction joints offset from panel joints that form messy horizontal lines, destroying the order of the whole exposed wall beyond correction. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b095-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「模板面材、脫模劑與表面顏色」與「配比、單一材料來源與色差控制」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Form facing, release agent and surface colour\" and \"Mix design, single-source materials and colour control\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b095-v13-09","title":"模板面材、脫模劑與表面顏色：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Form facing, release agent and surface colour: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「面板材料與脫模劑」如何影響清水混凝土模板與澆置的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Facing material and release agent” governs force, deformation or durability in “Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"混凝土表面會忠實複製模板面材的質感與吸水性：覆膜合板得到光滑均勻的表面，未處理木板留下木紋，吸水性不同的面板會讓表層水灰比不同而產生色差。ACI 347.3R 把模板面材特性列為成形面等級的三大分類之一。脫模劑塗太多會流淌並在表面留下深色斑痕或孔洞，塗太少則混凝土黏模；不同廠牌或批次的脫模劑也可能造成顏色差異。面材重複使用時表面磨損、吸水性改變，也會逐次改變混凝土顏色，所以高等級清水面要限制面材使用次數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「面板材料與脫模劑」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Concrete faithfully reproduces the texture and absorbency of the form facing: film-faced plywood gives a smooth, even surface, untreated boards leave wood grain, and facings of different absorbency change the surface water–cement ratio and cause colour differences. ACI 347.3R lists form-facing characteristics as one of its three surface-finish categories. Too much release agent runs and leaves dark stains or bugholes, too little lets concrete stick; different brands or batches of release agent can also change colour. Reused facings wear and change absorbency, gradually altering colour from use to use, so higher categories limit how many times a facing may be used. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Facing material and release agent” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：脫模劑用量若為 1 L/40 m²，1,000 m² 模板需 25 L，現場應以量杯或噴霧量控制而非目測。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: At 1 L of release agent per 40 m², 1,000 m² of form needs 25 L, controlled by measured spray rather than by eye.","failure":"常見誤解：「脫模劑塗得越多越好，可以保證拆模後表面光滑。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The more release agent the better; it guarantees a smooth surface after stripping.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「面板材料與脫模劑」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Facing material and release agent”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-09-k1","title":"模板面材、脫模劑與表面顏色","titleEn":"Form facing, release agent and surface colour","text":"混凝土表面會忠實複製模板面材的質感與吸水性：覆膜合板得到光滑均勻的表面，未處理木板留下木紋，吸水性不同的面板會讓表層水灰比不同而產生色差。ACI 347.3R 把模板面材特性列為成形面等級的三大分類之一。","textEn":"Concrete faithfully reproduces the texture and absorbency of the form facing: film-faced plywood gives a smooth, even surface, untreated boards leave wood grain, and facings of different absorbency change the surface water–cement ratio and cause colour differences. ACI 347.3R lists form-facing characteristics as one of its three surface-finish categories.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：脫模劑塗得越多越好，可以保證拆模後表面光滑。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The more release agent the better; it guarantees a smooth surface after stripping. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模板面材、脫模劑與表面顏色」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Form facing, release agent and surface colour\" is correct?","options":["混凝土表面會忠實複製模板面材的質感與吸水性：覆膜合板得到光滑均勻的表面，未處理木板留下木紋，吸水性不同的面板會讓表層水灰比不同而產生色差。","脫模劑塗得越多越好，可以保證拆模後表面光滑。","只要強度等級相同，不同預拌廠的混凝土在外觀上沒有差別。"],"optionsEn":["Concrete faithfully reproduces the texture and absorbency of the form facing: film-faced plywood gives a smooth, even surface, untreated boards leave wood grain, and facings of different absorbency change the surface water–cement ratio and cause colour differences.","The more release agent the better; it guarantees a smooth surface after stripping.","If the strength grade is the same, concrete from different plants looks the same."],"answer":0,"explanation":"混凝土表面會忠實複製模板面材的質感與吸水性：覆膜合板得到光滑均勻的表面，未處理木板留下木紋，吸水性不同的面板會讓表層水灰比不同而產生色差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Concrete faithfully reproduces the texture and absorbency of the form facing: film-faced plywood gives a smooth, even surface, untreated boards leave wood grain, and facings of different absorbency change the surface water–cement ratio and cause colour differences. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b095-v13-10","title":"模板面材、脫模劑與表面顏色：定量估算","titleEn":"Form facing, release agent and surface colour: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「面板材料與脫模劑」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Facing material and release agent” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：脫模劑用量若為 1 L/40 m²，1,000 m² 模板需 25 L，現場應以量杯或噴霧量控制而非目測。面材使用次數：清水牆總面積 2,400 m²、一套模板 400 m² 需翻用 2,400/400 = 6 次；若規格限定面材最多使用 4 次，需準備 6/4 = 1.5 套，即約 600 m² 面材。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: At 1 L of release agent per 40 m², 1,000 m² of form needs 25 L, controlled by measured spray rather than by eye. Facing reuse: 2,400 m² of exposed wall with a 400 m² form set means 2,400/400 = 6 uses; if the specification allows a facing to be used at most 4 times, 6/4 = 1.5 sets, about 600 m² of facing, are needed. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在樣板牆上試驗選定的面材與脫模劑組合，記錄用量與施作方式；施工中每次組模前檢查面材的損傷、修補與使用次數標記，並抽查脫模劑塗佈是否均勻，有流淌的面板須擦拭後才可合模。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Trial the chosen facing and release agent on the mock-up, recording dosage and application; before every assembly inspect facings for damage, repairs and use-count marks, spot-check that release agent is even, and wipe any panel with runs before closing the form.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"脫模劑用量若為 1 L/40 m²，1,000 m² 模板需 25 L，現場應以量杯或噴霧量控制而非目測。面材使用次數：清水牆總面積 2,400 m²、一套模板 400 m² 需翻用 2,400/400 = 6 次；若規格限定面材最多使用 4 次，需準備 6/4 = 1.5 套，即約 600 m² 面材。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"At 1 L of release agent per 40 m², 1,000 m² of form needs 25 L, controlled by measured spray rather than by eye. Facing reuse: 2,400 m² of exposed wall with a 400 m² form set means 2,400/400 = 6 uses; if the specification allows a facing to be used at most 4 times, 6/4 = 1.5 sets, about 600 m² of facing, are needed. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模板面材、脫模劑與表面顏色」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Form facing, release agent and surface colour\", which statement holds?","options":["清水混凝土澆得越快越連續，表面就越均勻。","脫模劑用量若為 1 L/40 m²，1,000 m² 模板需 25 L，現場應以量杯或噴霧量控制而非目測。","清水混凝土的外觀好壞只能靠主觀感覺判斷，無法量測。"],"optionsEn":["The faster and more continuously exposed concrete is placed, the more uniform the surface.","At 1 L of release agent per 40 m², 1,000 m² of form needs 25 L, controlled by measured spray rather than by eye.","The appearance of exposed concrete can only be judged subjectively and cannot be measured."],"answer":1,"explanation":"脫模劑用量若為 1 L/40 m²，1,000 m² 模板需 25 L，現場應以量杯或噴霧量控制而非目測。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"At 1 L of release agent per 40 m², 1,000 m² of form needs 25 L, controlled by measured spray rather than by eye. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b095-v13-11","title":"模板面材、脫模劑與表面顏色：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Form facing, release agent and surface colour: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「面板材料與脫模劑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Facing material and release agent” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在樣板牆上試驗選定的面材與脫模劑組合，記錄用量與施作方式；施工中每次組模前檢查面材的損傷、修補與使用次數標記，並抽查脫模劑塗佈是否均勻，有流淌的面板須擦拭後才可合模。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Trial the chosen facing and release agent on the mock-up, recording dosage and application; before every assembly inspect facings for damage, repairs and use-count marks, spot-check that release agent is even, and wipe any panel with runs before closing the form. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：規格中指定面材種類、使用次數上限與修補方式，以及脫模劑廠牌、用量與施作方法；同一可見面應使用同一批面材與同一批脫模劑，並在面板背面標記使用次數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Specify facing type, maximum uses and repair method, and release-agent brand, dosage and application in the specification; use one batch of facing and one batch of release agent for each visible face, and mark use counts on the back of each panel.","failure":"注意干擾：同一面牆混用新舊面材，新面板吸水多，牆面出現與面板分割相同的明暗格子；脫模劑過量在下方積聚，牆腳一帶出現深色斑塊與密集小孔，無法以清洗去除。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing new and used facings on one wall makes the more absorbent new panels show as a chequerboard of light and dark matching the panel layout; excess release agent pooling at the bottom leaves dark patches and dense small voids at the wall base that cannot be washed off. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在樣板牆上試驗選定的面材與脫模劑組合，記錄用量與施作方式；施工中每次組模前檢查面材的損傷、修補與使用次數標記，並抽查脫模劑塗佈是否均勻，有流淌的面板須擦拭後才可合模。","textEn":"Trial the chosen facing and release agent on the mock-up, recording dosage and application; before every assembly inspect facings for damage, repairs and use-count marks, spot-check that release agent is even, and wipe any panel with runs before closing the form.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"規格中指定面材種類、使用次數上限與修補方式，以及脫模劑廠牌、用量與施作方法；同一可見面應使用同一批面材與同一批脫模劑，並在面板背面標記使用次數。","textEn":"Specify facing type, maximum uses and repair method, and release-agent brand, dosage and application in the specification; use one batch of facing and one batch of release agent for each visible face, and mark use counts on the back of each panel.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模板面材、脫模劑與表面顏色」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Form facing, release agent and surface colour\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","清水混凝土弄髒了用高壓水柱沖洗就能恢復原貌。","在樣板牆上試驗選定的面材與脫模劑組合，記錄用量與施作方式。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Dirty exposed concrete can be restored to its original look by pressure washing.","Trial the chosen facing and release agent on the mock-up, recording dosage and application."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在樣板牆上試驗選定的面材與脫模劑組合，記錄用量與施作方式；施工中每次組模前檢查面材的損傷、修補與使用次數標記，並抽查脫模劑塗佈是否均勻，有流淌的面板須擦拭後才可合模。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Trial the chosen facing and release agent on the mock-up, recording dosage and application; before every assembly inspect facings for damage, repairs and use-count marks, spot-check that release agent is even, and wipe any panel with runs before closing the form. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b095-v13-12","title":"模板面材、脫模劑與表面顏色：失效診斷","titleEn":"Form facing, release agent and surface colour: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「面板材料與脫模劑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Facing material and release agent” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"同一面牆混用新舊面材，新面板吸水多，牆面出現與面板分割相同的明暗格子；脫模劑過量在下方積聚，牆腳一帶出現深色斑塊與密集小孔，無法以清洗去除。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing new and used facings on one wall makes the more absorbent new panels show as a chequerboard of light and dark matching the panel layout; excess release agent pooling at the bottom leaves dark patches and dense small voids at the wall base that cannot be washed off. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：面材重複使用時表面磨損、吸水性改變，也會逐次改變混凝土顏色，所以高等級清水面要限制面材使用次數。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reused facings wear and change absorbency, gradually altering colour from use to use, so higher categories limit how many times a facing may be used.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「脫模劑塗得越多越好，可以保證拆模後表面光滑。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The more release agent the better; it guarantees a smooth surface after stripping.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"同一面牆混用新舊面材，新面板吸水多，牆面出現與面板分割相同的明暗格子；脫模劑過量在下方積聚，牆腳一帶出現深色斑塊與密集小孔，無法以清洗去除。","textEn":"Mixing new and used facings on one wall makes the more absorbent new panels show as a chequerboard of light and dark matching the panel layout; excess release agent pooling at the bottom leaves dark patches and dense small voids at the wall base that cannot be washed off.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模板面材、脫模劑與表面顏色」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Form facing, release agent and surface colour\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["同一面牆混用新舊面材，新面板吸水多，牆面出現與面板分割相同的明暗格子；脫模劑過量在下方積聚，牆腳一帶出現深色斑塊與密集小孔，無法以清洗去除。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只要強度等級相同，不同預拌廠的混凝土在外觀上沒有差別。"],"optionsEn":["Mixing new and used facings on one wall makes the more absorbent new panels show as a chequerboard of light and dark matching the panel layout.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","If the strength grade is the same, concrete from different plants looks the same."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一面牆混用新舊面材，新面板吸水多，牆面出現與面板分割相同的明暗格子；脫模劑過量在下方積聚，牆腳一帶出現深色斑塊與密集小孔，無法以清洗去除。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing new and used facings on one wall makes the more absorbent new panels show as a chequerboard of light and dark matching the panel layout; excess release agent pooling at the bottom leaves dark patches and dense small voids at the wall base that cannot be washed off. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b095-v13-13","title":"配比、單一材料來源與色差控制：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Mix design, single-source materials and colour control: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「配比與材料一致性」如何影響清水混凝土模板與澆置的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mix and material consistency” governs force, deformation or durability in “Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"清水混凝土的顏色由水泥、礦物摻料、細骨材的顏色與表層水灰比共同決定，所以整個工程應使用同一水泥廠、同一摻料來源與同一砂石來源，避免批次變化。沙克研究所的混凝土採用含火山灰的配比，產生偏暖的色調，康並在地下室以不同顏色的試驗牆比較配比；這說明配比本身就是外觀設計的一部分。最常被忽視的變數是骨材含水率：砂的含水率變動會改變實際用水量，表層水灰比升高時顏色變淺且孔洞增加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「配比與材料一致性」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The colour of exposed concrete comes from the cement, supplementary materials, fine aggregate and surface water–cement ratio together, so the whole job should use one cement plant, one supplementary-material source and one aggregate source to avoid batch variation. The Salk Institute used a mix containing volcanic ash that gives a warm tone, and Kahn compared mixes in differently coloured trial walls in the basement, showing that the mix itself is part of the visual design. The most overlooked variable is aggregate moisture: changes in sand moisture alter the actual water content, and a higher surface water–cement ratio lightens colour and increases voids. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Mix and material consistency” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：細骨材 800 kg/m³、含水率比假設高 1%，等於多加 8 L 水；水泥 350 kg/m³ 時水灰比由 0.45 變為 0.45 + 8/350 ≈ 0.473，增加約 0.023，足以在相鄰兩車之間造成可見色差。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With 800 kg/m³ of fine aggregate, moisture 1% above the assumed value adds 8 L of water; with 350 kg/m³ of cement the water–cement ratio rises from 0.45 to 0.45 + 8/350 ≈ 0.473, about 0.023 more, enough to cause a visible colour difference between adjacent truckloads.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要強度等級相同，不同預拌廠的混凝土在外觀上沒有差別。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the strength grade is the same, concrete from different plants looks the same.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「配比與材料一致性」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Mix and material consistency”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-13-k1","title":"配比、單一材料來源與色差控制","titleEn":"Mix design, single-source materials and colour control","text":"清水混凝土的顏色由水泥、礦物摻料、細骨材的顏色與表層水灰比共同決定，所以整個工程應使用同一水泥廠、同一摻料來源與同一砂石來源，避免批次變化。沙克研究所的混凝土採用含火山灰的配比，產生偏暖的色調，康並在地下室以不同顏色的試驗牆比較配比；這說明配比本身就是外觀設計的一部分。","textEn":"The colour of exposed concrete comes from the cement, supplementary materials, fine aggregate and surface water–cement ratio together, so the whole job should use one cement plant, one supplementary-material source and one aggregate source to avoid batch variation. The Salk Institute used a mix containing volcanic ash that gives a warm tone, and Kahn compared mixes in differently coloured trial walls in the basement, showing that the mix itself is part of the visual design.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要強度等級相同，不同預拌廠的混凝土在外觀上沒有差別。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the strength grade is the same, concrete from different plants looks the same. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「配比、單一材料來源與色差控制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mix design, single-source materials and colour control\" is correct?","options":["只要強度等級相同，不同預拌廠的混凝土在外觀上沒有差別。","清水混凝土的顏色由水泥、礦物摻料、細骨材的顏色與表層水灰比共同決定，所以整個工程應使用同一水泥廠、同一摻料來源與同一砂石來源，避免批次變化。","清水模板只要表面光滑就好，背楞間距照一般結構模板即可。"],"optionsEn":["If the strength grade is the same, concrete from different plants looks the same.","The colour of exposed concrete comes from the cement, supplementary materials, fine aggregate and surface water–cement ratio together, so the whole job should use one cement plant, one supplementary-material source and one aggregate source to avoid batch variation.","Exposed-concrete forms only need a smooth facing; stud spacing can follow ordinary structural forms."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清水混凝土的顏色由水泥、礦物摻料、細骨材的顏色與表層水灰比共同決定，所以整個工程應使用同一水泥廠、同一摻料來源與同一砂石來源，避免批次變化。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The colour of exposed concrete comes from the cement, supplementary materials, fine aggregate and surface water–cement ratio together, so the whole job should use one cement plant, one supplementary-material source and one aggregate source to avoid batch variation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b095-v13-14","title":"配比、單一材料來源與色差控制：定量估算","titleEn":"Mix design, single-source materials and colour control: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「配比與材料一致性」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mix and material consistency” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：細骨材 800 kg/m³、含水率比假設高 1%，等於多加 8 L 水；水泥 350 kg/m³ 時水灰比由 0.45 變為 0.45 + 8/350 ≈ 0.473，增加約 0.023，足以在相鄰兩車之間造成可見色差。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With 800 kg/m³ of fine aggregate, moisture 1% above the assumed value adds 8 L of water; with 350 kg/m³ of cement the water–cement ratio rises from 0.45 to 0.45 + 8/350 ≈ 0.473, about 0.023 more, enough to cause a visible colour difference between adjacent truckloads. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：預拌廠以含水率感測器或每班烘乾試驗即時修正用水量，並記錄每車的配比、含水率與出廠時間；工地每車檢查坍度或坍流度與溫度，與樣板牆使用的配比紀錄比對，偏離範圍的車次退回。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The batch plant corrects water in real time with moisture probes or oven-dry tests each shift and records mix, moisture and dispatch time for every truck; on site check slump or slump flow and temperature for every truck against the mock-up mix record and reject trucks outside the range.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"細骨材 800 kg/m³、含水率比假設高 1%，等於多加 8 L 水；水泥 350 kg/m³ 時水灰比由 0.45 變為 0.45 + 8/350 ≈ 0.473，增加約 0.023，足以在相鄰兩車之間造成可見色差。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With 800 kg/m³ of fine aggregate, moisture 1% above the assumed value adds 8 L of water; with 350 kg/m³ of cement the water–cement ratio rises from 0.45 to 0.45 + 8/350 ≈ 0.473, about 0.023 more, enough to cause a visible colour difference between adjacent truckloads. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「配比、單一材料來源與色差控制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mix design, single-source materials and colour control\", which statement holds?","options":["樣板牆只是給業主看的展示品，正式施工時不需要再參照。","清水混凝土很耐久，不需要任何表面保護與修補計畫。","細骨材 800 kg/m³、含水率比假設高 1%，等於多加 8 L 水。"],"optionsEn":["The mock-up is just a showpiece for the owner and need not be referred to during construction.","Exposed concrete is durable and needs no surface protection or repair plan.","With 800 kg/m³ of fine aggregate, moisture 1% above the assumed value adds 8 L of water."],"answer":2,"explanation":"細骨材 800 kg/m³、含水率比假設高 1%，等於多加 8 L 水；水泥 350 kg/m³ 時水灰比由 0.45 變為 0.45 + 8/350 ≈ 0.473，增加約 0.023，足以在相鄰兩車之間造成可見色差。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With 800 kg/m³ of fine aggregate, moisture 1% above the assumed value adds 8 L of water; with 350 kg/m³ of cement the water–cement ratio rises from 0.45 to 0.45 + 8/350 ≈ 0.473, about 0.023 more, enough to cause a visible colour difference between adjacent truckloads. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b095-v13-15","title":"配比、單一材料來源與色差控制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mix design, single-source materials and colour control: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「配比與材料一致性」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mix and material consistency” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"預拌廠以含水率感測器或每班烘乾試驗即時修正用水量，並記錄每車的配比、含水率與出廠時間；工地每車檢查坍度或坍流度與溫度，與樣板牆使用的配比紀錄比對，偏離範圍的車次退回。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The batch plant corrects water in real time with moisture probes or oven-dry tests each shift and records mix, moisture and dispatch time for every truck; on site check slump or slump flow and temperature for every truck against the mock-up mix record and reject trucks outside the range. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：清水混凝土的配比、水泥與骨材來源應在樣板牆核定後鎖定，供應契約中規定材料庫存與不可替換條款；任何變更都要重做樣板並經建築師同意。","observationEn":"Site practice: Lock the mix, cement and aggregate sources once the mock-up is approved, require stockpiles and no-substitution clauses in the supply contract, and redo the mock-up with the architect's approval for any change.","failure":"注意干擾：工程中途水泥廠更換或砂石來源改變，新舊混凝土交界出現明顯色帶；夏季砂料含水率波動而預拌廠未修正，同一面牆上下層顏色不同，修補無法消除。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Changing cement plant or aggregate source mid-job leaves a clear colour band where old and new concrete meet; summer swings in sand moisture not corrected at the plant give upper and lower lifts of one wall different colours that no repair can remove. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"預拌廠以含水率感測器或每班烘乾試驗即時修正用水量，並記錄每車的配比、含水率與出廠時間；工地每車檢查坍度或坍流度與溫度，與樣板牆使用的配比紀錄比對，偏離範圍的車次退回。","textEn":"The batch plant corrects water in real time with moisture probes or oven-dry tests each shift and records mix, moisture and dispatch time for every truck; on site check slump or slump flow and temperature for every truck against the mock-up mix record and reject trucks outside the range.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"清水混凝土的配比、水泥與骨材來源應在樣板牆核定後鎖定，供應契約中規定材料庫存與不可替換條款；任何變更都要重做樣板並經建築師同意。","textEn":"Lock the mix, cement and aggregate sources once the mock-up is approved, require stockpiles and no-substitution clauses in the supply contract, and redo the mock-up with the architect's approval for any change.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「配比、單一材料來源與色差控制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mix design, single-source materials and colour control\"?","options":["預拌廠以含水率感測器或每班烘乾試驗即時修正用水量，並記錄每車的配比、含水率與出廠時間。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","清水混凝土就是不粉刷的普通混凝土，不需要特別的規格。"],"optionsEn":["The batch plant corrects water in real time with moisture probes or oven-dry tests each shift and records mix, moisture and dispatch time for every truck.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Exposed concrete is just ordinary concrete left unpainted and needs no special specification."],"answer":0,"explanation":"預拌廠以含水率感測器或每班烘乾試驗即時修正用水量，並記錄每車的配比、含水率與出廠時間；工地每車檢查坍度或坍流度與溫度，與樣板牆使用的配比紀錄比對，偏離範圍的車次退回。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The batch plant corrects water in real time with moisture probes or oven-dry tests each shift and records mix, moisture and dispatch time for every truck; on site check slump or slump flow and temperature for every truck against the mock-up mix record and reject trucks outside the range. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b095-v13-16","title":"配比、單一材料來源與色差控制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mix design, single-source materials and colour control: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「配比與材料一致性」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mix and material consistency” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"工程中途水泥廠更換或砂石來源改變，新舊混凝土交界出現明顯色帶；夏季砂料含水率波動而預拌廠未修正，同一面牆上下層顏色不同，修補無法消除。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Changing cement plant or aggregate source mid-job leaves a clear colour band where old and new concrete meet; summer swings in sand moisture not corrected at the plant give upper and lower lifts of one wall different colours that no repair can remove. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：最常被忽視的變數是骨材含水率：砂的含水率變動會改變實際用水量，表層水灰比升高時顏色變淺且孔洞增加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The most overlooked variable is aggregate moisture: changes in sand moisture alter the actual water content, and a higher surface water–cement ratio lightens colour and increases voids.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要強度等級相同，不同預拌廠的混凝土在外觀上沒有差別。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the strength grade is the same, concrete from different plants looks the same.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"工程中途水泥廠更換或砂石來源改變，新舊混凝土交界出現明顯色帶；夏季砂料含水率波動而預拌廠未修正，同一面牆上下層顏色不同，修補無法消除。","textEn":"Changing cement plant or aggregate source mid-job leaves a clear colour band where old and new concrete meet; summer swings in sand moisture not corrected at the plant give upper and lower lifts of one wall different colours that no repair can remove.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「配比、單一材料來源與色差控制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mix design, single-source materials and colour control\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","工程中途水泥廠更換或砂石來源改變，新舊混凝土交界出現明顯色帶；夏季砂料含水率波動而預拌廠未修正，同一面牆上下層顏色不同，修補無法消除。","清水模板只要表面光滑就好，背楞間距照一般結構模板即可。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Changing cement plant or aggregate source mid-job leaves a clear colour band where old and new concrete meet.","Exposed-concrete forms only need a smooth facing; stud spacing can follow ordinary structural forms."],"answer":1,"explanation":"工程中途水泥廠更換或砂石來源改變，新舊混凝土交界出現明顯色帶；夏季砂料含水率波動而預拌廠未修正，同一面牆上下層顏色不同，修補無法消除。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Changing cement plant or aggregate source mid-job leaves a clear colour band where old and new concrete meet; summer swings in sand moisture not corrected at the plant give upper and lower lifts of one wall different colours that no repair can remove. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b095-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「模板勁度、拼縫密封與漏漿痕」與「澆置上升速度、分層與振搗」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Form stiffness, joint sealing and grout-loss marks\" and \"Rate of rise, layering and vibration\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b095-v13-17","title":"模板勁度、拼縫密封與漏漿痕：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Form stiffness, joint sealing and grout-loss marks: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「模板勁度與拼縫止漏」如何影響清水混凝土模板與澆置的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Form stiffness and joint sealing” governs force, deformation or durability in “Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"清水面要平整、拼縫要乾淨，模板必須夠剛且密封良好。新鮮混凝土的側壓使面板在支撐間撓曲，撓曲量若超過肉眼在斜光下可辨識的程度，牆面就會出現波浪；拼縫若有縫隙，水泥漿在壓力下從縫隙流失，留下砂紋、深色漏漿痕或粗糙的蜂窩帶。因此清水模板常比結構模板有更密的背楞、更厚的面板，拼縫以密封條或膠帶處理，牆角與施工縫以倒角或凹槽把無法避免的接縫變成刻意的線條。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「模板勁度與拼縫止漏」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For a flat face and clean joints, forms must be stiff and well sealed. Fresh-concrete pressure bends facings between supports, and if deflection exceeds what the eye detects in raking light the wall shows waves; any gap at a joint lets paste escape under pressure, leaving sand streaks, dark grout-loss lines or rough honeycomb bands. Exposed-concrete forms therefore often have closer studs and thicker facings than structural forms, joints sealed with gaskets or tape, and chamfers or reveals at corners and construction joints that turn unavoidable joints into deliberate lines. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Form stiffness and joint sealing” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：21 mm 合板、E = 7,000 MPa，每 mm 寬 I = 21³/12 ≈ 772 mm⁴；側壓 50 kPa（0.05 N/mm²）、背楞間距 300 mm 時 δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI) ≈ 0.98 mm ≈ L/307。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For 21 mm plywood with E = 7,000 MPa, I per mm width = 21³/12 ≈ 772 mm⁴; at 50 kPa (0.05 N/mm²) with studs at 300 mm, δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI) ≈ 0.98 mm ≈ L/307.","failure":"常見誤解：「清水模板只要表面光滑就好，背楞間距照一般結構模板即可。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Exposed-concrete forms only need a smooth facing; stud spacing can follow ordinary structural forms.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「模板勁度與拼縫止漏」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Form stiffness and joint sealing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-17-k1","title":"模板勁度、拼縫密封與漏漿痕","titleEn":"Form stiffness, joint sealing and grout-loss marks","text":"清水面要平整、拼縫要乾淨，模板必須夠剛且密封良好。新鮮混凝土的側壓使面板在支撐間撓曲，撓曲量若超過肉眼在斜光下可辨識的程度，牆面就會出現波浪；拼縫若有縫隙，水泥漿在壓力下從縫隙流失，留下砂紋、深色漏漿痕或粗糙的蜂窩帶。","textEn":"For a flat face and clean joints, forms must be stiff and well sealed. Fresh-concrete pressure bends facings between supports, and if deflection exceeds what the eye detects in raking light the wall shows waves; any gap at a joint lets paste escape under pressure, leaving sand streaks, dark grout-loss lines or rough honeycomb bands.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：清水模板只要表面光滑就好，背楞間距照一般結構模板即可。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Exposed-concrete forms only need a smooth facing; stud spacing can follow ordinary structural forms. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「模板勁度、拼縫密封與漏漿痕」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Form stiffness, joint sealing and grout-loss marks\" is correct?","options":["清水模板只要表面光滑就好，背楞間距照一般結構模板即可。","清水混凝土澆得越快越連續，表面就越均勻。","清水面要平整、拼縫要乾淨，模板必須夠剛且密封良好。"],"optionsEn":["Exposed-concrete forms only need a smooth facing; stud spacing can follow ordinary structural forms.","The faster and more continuously exposed concrete is placed, the more uniform the surface.","For a flat face and clean joints, forms must be stiff and well sealed."],"answer":2,"explanation":"清水面要平整、拼縫要乾淨，模板必須夠剛且密封良好。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For a flat face and clean joints, forms must be stiff and well sealed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b095-v13-18","title":"模板勁度、拼縫密封與漏漿痕：定量估算","titleEn":"Form stiffness, joint sealing and grout-loss marks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「模板勁度與拼縫止漏」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Form stiffness and joint sealing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：21 mm 合板、E = 7,000 MPa，每 mm 寬 I = 21³/12 ≈ 772 mm⁴；側壓 50 kPa（0.05 N/mm²）、背楞間距 300 mm 時 δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI) ≈ 0.98 mm ≈ L/307。若要求 L/400，背楞間距須 ≤ 約 281 mm；取 250 mm 時 δ ≈ 0.47 mm（約 L/531）。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For 21 mm plywood with E = 7,000 MPa, I per mm width = 21³/12 ≈ 772 mm⁴; at 50 kPa (0.05 N/mm²) with studs at 300 mm, δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI) ≈ 0.98 mm ≈ L/307. Meeting L/400 needs stud spacing ≤ about 281 mm; at 250 mm δ ≈ 0.47 mm, about L/531. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：模板計算書須列出設計側壓、面板與背楞的撓度限值；組模後以直尺與燈光斜照檢查面板平整，拼縫以塞尺確認間隙並檢查密封材；澆置中派人在模板外側巡視漏漿，發現時立即處理。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The formwork calculations must state design pressure and deflection limits for facings and studs; after assembly check flatness with a straightedge and raking light, gauge joint gaps with feelers and inspect seals; during placing have someone patrol the outside of the forms for paste leaks and deal with them at once.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"21 mm 合板、E = 7,000 MPa，每 mm 寬 I = 21³/12 ≈ 772 mm⁴；側壓 50 kPa（0.05 N/mm²）、背楞間距 300 mm 時 δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI) ≈ 0.98 mm ≈ L/307。若要求 L/400，背楞間距須 ≤ 約 281 mm；取 250 mm 時 δ ≈ 0.47 mm（約 L/531）。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For 21 mm plywood with E = 7,000 MPa, I per mm width = 21³/12 ≈ 772 mm⁴; at 50 kPa (0.05 N/mm²) with studs at 300 mm, δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI) ≈ 0.98 mm ≈ L/307. Meeting L/400 needs stud spacing ≤ about 281 mm; at 250 mm δ ≈ 0.47 mm, about L/531. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「模板勁度、拼縫密封與漏漿痕」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Form stiffness, joint sealing and grout-loss marks\", which statement holds?","options":["21 mm 合板、E = 7,000 MPa，每 mm 寬 I = 21³/12 ≈ 772 mm⁴。","清水混凝土的外觀好壞只能靠主觀感覺判斷，無法量測。","清水混凝土弄髒了用高壓水柱沖洗就能恢復原貌。"],"optionsEn":["For 21 mm plywood with E = 7,000 MPa, I per mm width = 21³/12 ≈ 772 mm⁴; at 50 kPa (0.05 N/mm²) with studs at 300 mm, δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI) ≈ 0.98 mm ≈ L/307.","The appearance of exposed concrete can only be judged subjectively and cannot be measured.","Dirty exposed concrete can be restored to its original look by pressure washing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"21 mm 合板、E = 7,000 MPa，每 mm 寬 I = 21³/12 ≈ 772 mm⁴；側壓 50 kPa（0.05 N/mm²）、背楞間距 300 mm 時 δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI) ≈ 0.98 mm ≈ L/307。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For 21 mm plywood with E = 7,000 MPa, I per mm width = 21³/12 ≈ 772 mm⁴; at 50 kPa (0.05 N/mm²) with studs at 300 mm, δ = 5wL⁴/(384EI) ≈ 0.98 mm ≈ L/307. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b095-v13-19","title":"模板勁度、拼縫密封與漏漿痕：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Form stiffness, joint sealing and grout-loss marks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「模板勁度與拼縫止漏」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Form stiffness and joint sealing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"模板計算書須列出設計側壓、面板與背楞的撓度限值；組模後以直尺與燈光斜照檢查面板平整，拼縫以塞尺確認間隙並檢查密封材；澆置中派人在模板外側巡視漏漿，發現時立即處理。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The formwork calculations must state design pressure and deflection limits for facings and studs; after assembly check flatness with a straightedge and raking light, gauge joint gaps with feelers and inspect seals; during placing have someone patrol the outside of the forms for paste leaks and deal with them at once. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：清水模板的撓度限值、拼縫密封方式與倒角凹槽詳圖要寫入模板設計規範，並由模板設計者出具計算書；第一次使用的模板系統必須先在樣板牆上驗證。","observationEn":"Site practice: Write deflection limits, joint-sealing methods and chamfer and reveal details for exposed-concrete forms into the formwork specification, with calculations from the formwork designer, and prove any formwork system on the mock-up before first use.","failure":"注意干擾：為節省材料放寬背楞間距，拆模後在斜光下牆面出現規則的波浪；拼縫未密封，每一道拼縫兩側都有砂紋與深色漏漿線，牆腳因壓力最大而出現連續蜂窩帶。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Widening stud spacing to save material leaves regular waves visible in raking light after stripping; unsealed joints leave sand streaks and dark leak lines along every joint, and the wall base, where pressure is greatest, shows a continuous honeycomb band. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"模板計算書須列出設計側壓、面板與背楞的撓度限值；組模後以直尺與燈光斜照檢查面板平整，拼縫以塞尺確認間隙並檢查密封材；澆置中派人在模板外側巡視漏漿，發現時立即處理。","textEn":"The formwork calculations must state design pressure and deflection limits for facings and studs; after assembly check flatness with a straightedge and raking light, gauge joint gaps with feelers and inspect seals; during placing have someone patrol the outside of the forms for paste leaks and deal with them at once.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"清水模板的撓度限值、拼縫密封方式與倒角凹槽詳圖要寫入模板設計規範，並由模板設計者出具計算書；第一次使用的模板系統必須先在樣板牆上驗證。","textEn":"Write deflection limits, joint-sealing methods and chamfer and reveal details for exposed-concrete forms into the formwork specification, with calculations from the formwork designer, and prove any formwork system on the mock-up before first use.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「模板勁度、拼縫密封與漏漿痕」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Form stiffness, joint sealing and grout-loss marks\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","模板計算書須列出設計側壓、面板與背楞的撓度限值。","模板拼縫與繫桿孔只是施工痕跡，交給工地自行安排即可。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","The formwork calculations must state design pressure and deflection limits for facings and studs.","Form joints and tie holes are just construction marks that the site can arrange as it likes."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模板計算書須列出設計側壓、面板與背楞的撓度限值；組模後以直尺與燈光斜照檢查面板平整，拼縫以塞尺確認間隙並檢查密封材；澆置中派人在模板外側巡視漏漿，發現時立即處理。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The formwork calculations must state design pressure and deflection limits for facings and studs; after assembly check flatness with a straightedge and raking light, gauge joint gaps with feelers and inspect seals; during placing have someone patrol the outside of the forms for paste leaks and deal with them at once. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b095-v13-20","title":"模板勁度、拼縫密封與漏漿痕：失效診斷","titleEn":"Form stiffness, joint sealing and grout-loss marks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「模板勁度與拼縫止漏」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Form stiffness and joint sealing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為節省材料放寬背楞間距，拆模後在斜光下牆面出現規則的波浪；拼縫未密封，每一道拼縫兩側都有砂紋與深色漏漿線，牆腳因壓力最大而出現連續蜂窩帶。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Widening stud spacing to save material leaves regular waves visible in raking light after stripping; unsealed joints leave sand streaks and dark leak lines along every joint, and the wall base, where pressure is greatest, shows a continuous honeycomb band. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此清水模板常比結構模板有更密的背楞、更厚的面板，拼縫以密封條或膠帶處理，牆角與施工縫以倒角或凹槽把無法避免的接縫變成刻意的線條。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Exposed-concrete forms therefore often have closer studs and thicker facings than structural forms, joints sealed with gaskets or tape, and chamfers or reveals at corners and construction joints that turn unavoidable joints into deliberate lines.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「清水模板只要表面光滑就好，背楞間距照一般結構模板即可。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Exposed-concrete forms only need a smooth facing; stud spacing can follow ordinary structural forms.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為節省材料放寬背楞間距，拆模後在斜光下牆面出現規則的波浪；拼縫未密封，每一道拼縫兩側都有砂紋與深色漏漿線，牆腳因壓力最大而出現連續蜂窩帶。","textEn":"Widening stud spacing to save material leaves regular waves visible in raking light after stripping; unsealed joints leave sand streaks and dark leak lines along every joint, and the wall base, where pressure is greatest, shows a continuous honeycomb band.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「模板勁度、拼縫密封與漏漿痕」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Form stiffness, joint sealing and grout-loss marks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","清水混凝土澆得越快越連續，表面就越均勻。","為節省材料放寬背楞間距，拆模後在斜光下牆面出現規則的波浪；拼縫未密封，每一道拼縫兩側都有砂紋與深色漏漿線，牆腳因壓力最大而出現連續蜂窩帶。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The faster and more continuously exposed concrete is placed, the more uniform the surface.","Widening stud spacing to save material leaves regular waves visible in raking light after stripping."],"answer":2,"explanation":"為節省材料放寬背楞間距，拆模後在斜光下牆面出現規則的波浪；拼縫未密封，每一道拼縫兩側都有砂紋與深色漏漿線，牆腳因壓力最大而出現連續蜂窩帶。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Widening stud spacing to save material leaves regular waves visible in raking light after stripping; unsealed joints leave sand streaks and dark leak lines along every joint, and the wall base, where pressure is greatest, shows a continuous honeycomb band. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b095-v13-21","title":"澆置上升速度、分層與振搗：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Rate of rise, layering and vibration: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「澆置速度與振搗控制」如何影響清水混凝土模板與澆置的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Placing rate and vibration control” governs force, deformation or durability in “Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"清水牆的澆置要控制「上升速度」，也就是單位時間內混凝土在模板中升高的高度；它同時決定模板側壓、分層結合與表面氣泡。上升太快時側壓接近液壓，模板撓曲與漏漿增加，下層混凝土也來不及排出氣泡；太慢則兩層之間可能形成顏色不同的層線。振搗要讓氣泡沿模板面上升排出，但過度振搗會使漿體上浮、骨材下沉，造成上下顏色不同；振動棒碰觸模板面會在表面留下磨痕。ACI 347.3R 把表面孔洞比例作為成形面等級的分類依據之一，振搗正是控制孔洞的關鍵。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「澆置速度與振搗控制」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Placing exposed walls means controlling the rate of rise, how fast concrete climbs in the form, which governs form pressure, bonding between layers and surface bubbles. Too fast and pressure approaches hydrostatic, form deflection and leaks increase and lower layers cannot release air; too slow and colour lines may form between layers. Vibration must drive bubbles up and out along the form face, but over-vibration floats paste up and sinks aggregate, giving different colours top and bottom, and a vibrator touching the facing scuffs the surface. ACI 347.3R uses surface void ratio as one of its classification criteria, and vibration is the key to controlling voids. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Placing rate and vibration control” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：牆長 12 m、厚 0.3 m，預拌車以 15 m³/h 供料時上升速度 = 15/(12×0.3) ≈ 4.17 m/h，遠高於模板設計所假設的 1.5 m/h；要維持 1.5 m/h，供料應限制為 1.5×12×0.3 = 5.4 m³/h，5.46 m 高的牆需約 3.6 h 完成。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a wall 12 m long and 0.3 m thick, supplying 15 m³/h gives a rate of rise of 15/(12×0.3) ≈ 4.17 m/h, far above the 1.5 m/h assumed in the formwork design; holding 1.5 m/h limits supply to 1.5×12×0.3 = 5.4 m³/h, and a 5.46 m wall takes about 3.6 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「清水混凝土澆得越快越連續，表面就越均勻。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The faster and more continuously exposed concrete is placed, the more uniform the surface.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「澆置速度與振搗控制」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Placing rate and vibration control”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-21-k1","title":"澆置上升速度、分層與振搗","titleEn":"Rate of rise, layering and vibration","text":"清水牆的澆置要控制「上升速度」，也就是單位時間內混凝土在模板中升高的高度；它同時決定模板側壓、分層結合與表面氣泡。上升太快時側壓接近液壓，模板撓曲與漏漿增加，下層混凝土也來不及排出氣泡；太慢則兩層之間可能形成顏色不同的層線。","textEn":"Placing exposed walls means controlling the rate of rise, how fast concrete climbs in the form, which governs form pressure, bonding between layers and surface bubbles. Too fast and pressure approaches hydrostatic, form deflection and leaks increase and lower layers cannot release air; too slow and colour lines may form between layers.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：清水混凝土澆得越快越連續，表面就越均勻。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The faster and more continuously exposed concrete is placed, the more uniform the surface. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「澆置上升速度、分層與振搗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rate of rise, layering and vibration\" is correct?","options":["清水牆的澆置要控制「上升速度」，也就是單位時間內混凝土在模板中升高的高度；它同時決定模板側壓、分層結合與表面氣泡。","清水混凝土澆得越快越連續，表面就越均勻。","樣板牆只是給業主看的展示品，正式施工時不需要再參照。"],"optionsEn":["Placing exposed walls means controlling the rate of rise, how fast concrete climbs in the form, which governs form pressure, bonding between layers and surface bubbles.","The faster and more continuously exposed concrete is placed, the more uniform the surface.","The mock-up is just a showpiece for the owner and need not be referred to during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"清水牆的澆置要控制「上升速度」，也就是單位時間內混凝土在模板中升高的高度；它同時決定模板側壓、分層結合與表面氣泡。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Placing exposed walls means controlling the rate of rise, how fast concrete climbs in the form, which governs form pressure, bonding between layers and surface bubbles. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b095-v13-22","title":"澆置上升速度、分層與振搗：定量估算","titleEn":"Rate of rise, layering and vibration: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「澆置速度與振搗控制」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Placing rate and vibration control” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：牆長 12 m、厚 0.3 m，預拌車以 15 m³/h 供料時上升速度 = 15/(12×0.3) ≈ 4.17 m/h，遠高於模板設計所假設的 1.5 m/h；要維持 1.5 m/h，供料應限制為 1.5×12×0.3 = 5.4 m³/h，5.46 m 高的牆需約 3.6 h 完成。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a wall 12 m long and 0.3 m thick, supplying 15 m³/h gives a rate of rise of 15/(12×0.3) ≈ 4.17 m/h, far above the 1.5 m/h assumed in the formwork design; holding 1.5 m/h limits supply to 1.5×12×0.3 = 5.4 m³/h, and a 5.46 m wall takes about 3.6 h. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：澆置計畫列出每道牆的上升速度上限、分層厚度、澆置點與振動棒插入間距，現場以時間與液面高度紀錄核對上升速度；樣板牆上試驗振搗時間與插入方式，並以相同人員與設備施作正式牆體。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The placing plan lists maximum rate of rise, layer thickness, pour points and vibrator spacing for each wall, and the site checks rate of rise from time and level records; trial vibration time and technique on the mock-up and use the same crew and equipment for the real walls.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"牆長 12 m、厚 0.3 m，預拌車以 15 m³/h 供料時上升速度 = 15/(12×0.3) ≈ 4.17 m/h，遠高於模板設計所假設的 1.5 m/h；要維持 1.5 m/h，供料應限制為 1.5×12×0.3 = 5.4 m³/h，5.46 m 高的牆需約 3.6 h 完成。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"For a wall 12 m long and 0.3 m thick, supplying 15 m³/h gives a rate of rise of 15/(12×0.3) ≈ 4.17 m/h, far above the 1.5 m/h assumed in the formwork design; holding 1.5 m/h limits supply to 1.5×12×0.3 = 5.4 m³/h, and a 5.46 m wall takes about 3.6 h. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「澆置上升速度、分層與振搗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rate of rise, layering and vibration\", which statement holds?","options":["清水混凝土很耐久，不需要任何表面保護與修補計畫。","牆長 12 m、厚 0.3 m，預拌車以 15 m³/h 供料時上升速度 = 15/(12×0.3) ≈ 4.17 m/h，遠高於模板設計所假設的 1.5 m/h。","清水混凝土就是不粉刷的普通混凝土，不需要特別的規格。"],"optionsEn":["Exposed concrete is durable and needs no surface protection or repair plan.","For a wall 12 m long and 0.3 m thick, supplying 15 m³/h gives a rate of rise of 15/(12×0.3) ≈ 4.17 m/h, far above the 1.5 m/h assumed in the formwork design.","Exposed concrete is just ordinary concrete left unpainted and needs no special specification."],"answer":1,"explanation":"牆長 12 m、厚 0.3 m，預拌車以 15 m³/h 供料時上升速度 = 15/(12×0.3) ≈ 4.17 m/h，遠高於模板設計所假設的 1.5 m/h；要維持 1.5 m/h，供料應限制為 1.5×12×0.3 = 5.4 m³/h，5.46 m 高的牆需約 3.6 h 完成。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a wall 12 m long and 0.3 m thick, supplying 15 m³/h gives a rate of rise of 15/(12×0.3) ≈ 4.17 m/h, far above the 1.5 m/h assumed in the formwork design; holding 1.5 m/h limits supply to 1.5×12×0.3 = 5.4 m³/h, and a 5.46 m wall takes about 3.6 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b095-v13-23","title":"澆置上升速度、分層與振搗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rate of rise, layering and vibration: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「澆置速度與振搗控制」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Placing rate and vibration control” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"澆置計畫列出每道牆的上升速度上限、分層厚度、澆置點與振動棒插入間距，現場以時間與液面高度紀錄核對上升速度；樣板牆上試驗振搗時間與插入方式，並以相同人員與設備施作正式牆體。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The placing plan lists maximum rate of rise, layer thickness, pour points and vibrator spacing for each wall, and the site checks rate of rise from time and level records; trial vibration time and technique on the mock-up and use the same crew and equipment for the real walls. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：清水牆澆置由經過樣板訓練的固定班組執行，並安排專人控制供料節奏與記錄上升速度；澆置前在交底會議說明振動棒操作規則（垂直插入、不碰模板、規定停留時間）。","observationEn":"Site practice: Have exposed walls placed by a fixed crew trained on the mock-up, with a person assigned to pace supply and log the rate of rise; brief the vibrator rules at the pre-pour meeting: insert vertically, never touch the facing, hold for the specified time.","failure":"注意干擾：為趕在下班前完成而加快供料，上升速度倍增，模板鼓脹、拼縫漏漿，牆面下半部出現大量氣泡孔；振動棒在模板面附近反覆拖動，表面留下弧形磨痕與砂紋。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Speeding up supply to finish before the end of shift doubles the rate of rise, bulging the forms and leaking at joints, and leaves many bugholes on the lower half of the wall; dragging the vibrator back and forth near the facing leaves arc-shaped scuff marks and sand streaks. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"澆置計畫列出每道牆的上升速度上限、分層厚度、澆置點與振動棒插入間距，現場以時間與液面高度紀錄核對上升速度；樣板牆上試驗振搗時間與插入方式，並以相同人員與設備施作正式牆體。","textEn":"The placing plan lists maximum rate of rise, layer thickness, pour points and vibrator spacing for each wall, and the site checks rate of rise from time and level records; trial vibration time and technique on the mock-up and use the same crew and equipment for the real walls.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"清水牆澆置由經過樣板訓練的固定班組執行，並安排專人控制供料節奏與記錄上升速度；澆置前在交底會議說明振動棒操作規則（垂直插入、不碰模板、規定停留時間）。","textEn":"Have exposed walls placed by a fixed crew trained on the mock-up, with a person assigned to pace supply and log the rate of rise; brief the vibrator rules at the pre-pour meeting: insert vertically, never touch the facing, hold for the specified time.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「澆置上升速度、分層與振搗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rate of rise, layering and vibration\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","脫模劑塗得越多越好，可以保證拆模後表面光滑。","澆置計畫列出每道牆的上升速度上限、分層厚度、澆置點與振動棒插入間距，現場以時間與液面高度紀錄核對上升速度。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The more release agent the better; it guarantees a smooth surface after stripping.","The placing plan lists maximum rate of rise, layer thickness, pour points and vibrator spacing for each wall, and the site checks rate of rise from time and level records."],"answer":2,"explanation":"澆置計畫列出每道牆的上升速度上限、分層厚度、澆置點與振動棒插入間距，現場以時間與液面高度紀錄核對上升速度；樣板牆上試驗振搗時間與插入方式，並以相同人員與設備施作正式牆體。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The placing plan lists maximum rate of rise, layer thickness, pour points and vibrator spacing for each wall, and the site checks rate of rise from time and level records; trial vibration time and technique on the mock-up and use the same crew and equipment for the real walls. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b095-v13-24","title":"澆置上升速度、分層與振搗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rate of rise, layering and vibration: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「澆置速度與振搗控制」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Placing rate and vibration control” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"為趕在下班前完成而加快供料，上升速度倍增，模板鼓脹、拼縫漏漿，牆面下半部出現大量氣泡孔；振動棒在模板面附近反覆拖動，表面留下弧形磨痕與砂紋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Speeding up supply to finish before the end of shift doubles the rate of rise, bulging the forms and leaking at joints, and leaves many bugholes on the lower half of the wall; dragging the vibrator back and forth near the facing leaves arc-shaped scuff marks and sand streaks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：ACI 347.3R 把表面孔洞比例作為成形面等級的分類依據之一，振搗正是控制孔洞的關鍵。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: ACI 347.3R uses surface void ratio as one of its classification criteria, and vibration is the key to controlling voids.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「清水混凝土澆得越快越連續，表面就越均勻。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The faster and more continuously exposed concrete is placed, the more uniform the surface.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"為趕在下班前完成而加快供料，上升速度倍增，模板鼓脹、拼縫漏漿，牆面下半部出現大量氣泡孔；振動棒在模板面附近反覆拖動，表面留下弧形磨痕與砂紋。","textEn":"Speeding up supply to finish before the end of shift doubles the rate of rise, bulging the forms and leaking at joints, and leaves many bugholes on the lower half of the wall; dragging the vibrator back and forth near the facing leaves arc-shaped scuff marks and sand streaks.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「澆置上升速度、分層與振搗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rate of rise, layering and vibration\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["為趕在下班前完成而加快供料，上升速度倍增，模板鼓脹、拼縫漏漿，牆面下半部出現大量氣泡孔；振動棒在模板面附近反覆拖動，表面留下弧形磨痕與砂紋。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","樣板牆只是給業主看的展示品，正式施工時不需要再參照。"],"optionsEn":["Speeding up supply to finish before the end of shift doubles the rate of rise, bulging the forms and leaking at joints, and leaves many bugholes on the lower half of the wall.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","The mock-up is just a showpiece for the owner and need not be referred to during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"為趕在下班前完成而加快供料，上升速度倍增，模板鼓脹、拼縫漏漿，牆面下半部出現大量氣泡孔；振動棒在模板面附近反覆拖動，表面留下弧形磨痕與砂紋。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Speeding up supply to finish before the end of shift doubles the rate of rise, bulging the forms and leaking at joints, and leaves many bugholes on the lower half of the wall; dragging the vibrator back and forth near the facing leaves arc-shaped scuff marks and sand streaks. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b095-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「樣板牆、比對基準與驗收距離」與「色差、平整度與孔洞的量化檢測」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Mock-up, reference standard and viewing distance\" and \"Quantifying colour, flatness and voids\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b095-v13-25","title":"樣板牆、比對基準與驗收距離：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Mock-up, reference standard and viewing distance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「樣板牆與觀看距離」如何影響清水混凝土模板與澆置的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mock-up and viewing distance” governs force, deformation or durability in “Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"清水混凝土的驗收離不開樣板牆。ACI 347.3R 把樣板定義為依契約文件製作的構件樣本，用來建立預期的表面完成度；它同時驗證模板、配比、脫模劑、澆置與振搗的組合，並成為整個工程的比對基準。樣板牆應包含真實的拼縫、繫桿孔、轉角、施工縫與開口邊緣，並在與正式工程相同的季節與條件下製作。驗收時還必須規定觀看距離與光線條件：同一面牆在 1 m 與 10 m 外看，可接受的缺陷完全不同。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「樣板牆與觀看距離」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Acceptance of exposed concrete depends on the mock-up. ACI 347.3R defines a mock-up as a sample of a building component made as specified in the contract documents to establish the expected surface finish; it proves the combination of forms, mix, release agent, placing and vibration and becomes the reference for the whole job. A mock-up should include real panel joints, tie holes, a corner, a construction joint and an opening edge, and be cast in the same season and conditions as the work. Acceptance must also state viewing distance and light: the same wall seen from 1 m and from 10 m tolerates entirely different defects. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Mock-up and viewing distance” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：人眼解析度約 1 角分，觀看距離 d 時可分辨尺寸 ≈ d·tan(1/60°)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Human visual resolution is about one arc-minute, so the resolvable size at distance d is about d·tan(1/60°).","failure":"常見誤解：「樣板牆只是給業主看的展示品，正式施工時不需要再參照。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The mock-up is just a showpiece for the owner and need not be referred to during construction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「樣板牆與觀看距離」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Mock-up and viewing distance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-25-k1","title":"樣板牆、比對基準與驗收距離","titleEn":"Mock-up, reference standard and viewing distance","text":"清水混凝土的驗收離不開樣板牆。ACI 347.3R 把樣板定義為依契約文件製作的構件樣本，用來建立預期的表面完成度；它同時驗證模板、配比、脫模劑、澆置與振搗的組合，並成為整個工程的比對基準。","textEn":"Acceptance of exposed concrete depends on the mock-up. ACI 347.3R defines a mock-up as a sample of a building component made as specified in the contract documents to establish the expected surface finish; it proves the combination of forms, mix, release agent, placing and vibration and becomes the reference for the whole job.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：樣板牆只是給業主看的展示品，正式施工時不需要再參照。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The mock-up is just a showpiece for the owner and need not be referred to during construction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樣板牆、比對基準與驗收距離」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mock-up, reference standard and viewing distance\" is correct?","options":["樣板牆只是給業主看的展示品，正式施工時不需要再參照。","清水混凝土的驗收離不開樣板牆。","清水混凝土的外觀好壞只能靠主觀感覺判斷，無法量測。"],"optionsEn":["The mock-up is just a showpiece for the owner and need not be referred to during construction.","Acceptance of exposed concrete depends on the mock-up.","The appearance of exposed concrete can only be judged subjectively and cannot be measured."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清水混凝土的驗收離不開樣板牆。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Acceptance of exposed concrete depends on the mock-up. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b095-v13-26","title":"樣板牆、比對基準與驗收距離：定量估算","titleEn":"Mock-up, reference standard and viewing distance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樣板牆與觀看距離」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mock-up and viewing distance” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：人眼解析度約 1 角分，觀看距離 d 時可分辨尺寸 ≈ d·tan(1/60°)。d = 6 m 時約 6,000×0.000291 ≈ 1.75 mm，表示 1 mm 以下的小氣孔在 6 m 外幾乎看不見；若改為 1 m 近看，可分辨約 0.29 mm，驗收結果會完全不同。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Human visual resolution is about one arc-minute, so the resolvable size at distance d is about d·tan(1/60°). At d = 6 m that is about 6,000×0.000291 ≈ 1.75 mm, so bugholes under 1 mm are almost invisible from 6 m; from 1 m about 0.29 mm can be resolved and the acceptance outcome changes completely. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：樣板牆完成後由業主、建築師、結構工程師與承包商在規定距離與自然光下共同檢視並書面核定，拍照存檔；正式工程驗收時在相同距離與光線下與樣板牆並列比較，爭議部分以檢查框量測孔洞比例與色差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Once the mock-up is complete, owner, architect, structural engineer and contractor inspect it together at the specified distance in daylight, approve it in writing and photograph it; at acceptance compare the work side by side with the mock-up at the same distance and light, settling disputes with void-ratio and colour measurements in an inspection frame.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"人眼解析度約 1 角分，觀看距離 d 時可分辨尺寸 ≈ d·tan(1/60°)。d = 6 m 時約 6,000×0.000291 ≈ 1.75 mm，表示 1 mm 以下的小氣孔在 6 m 外幾乎看不見；若改為 1 m 近看，可分辨約 0.29 mm，驗收結果會完全不同。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Human visual resolution is about one arc-minute, so the resolvable size at distance d is about d·tan(1/60°). At d = 6 m that is about 6,000×0.000291 ≈ 1.75 mm, so bugholes under 1 mm are almost invisible from 6 m; from 1 m about 0.29 mm can be resolved and the acceptance outcome changes completely. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樣板牆、比對基準與驗收距離」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mock-up, reference standard and viewing distance\", which statement holds?","options":["清水混凝土弄髒了用高壓水柱沖洗就能恢復原貌。","模板拼縫與繫桿孔只是施工痕跡，交給工地自行安排即可。","人眼解析度約 1 角分，觀看距離 d 時可分辨尺寸 ≈ d·tan(1/60°)。"],"optionsEn":["Dirty exposed concrete can be restored to its original look by pressure washing.","Form joints and tie holes are just construction marks that the site can arrange as it likes.","Human visual resolution is about one arc-minute, so the resolvable size at distance d is about d·tan(1/60°)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"人眼解析度約 1 角分，觀看距離 d 時可分辨尺寸 ≈ d·tan(1/60°)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Human visual resolution is about one arc-minute, so the resolvable size at distance d is about d·tan(1/60°). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b095-v13-27","title":"樣板牆、比對基準與驗收距離：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mock-up, reference standard and viewing distance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「樣板牆與觀看距離」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mock-up and viewing distance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"樣板牆完成後由業主、建築師、結構工程師與承包商在規定距離與自然光下共同檢視並書面核定，拍照存檔；正式工程驗收時在相同距離與光線下與樣板牆並列比較，爭議部分以檢查框量測孔洞比例與色差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Once the mock-up is complete, owner, architect, structural engineer and contractor inspect it together at the specified distance in daylight, approve it in writing and photograph it; at acceptance compare the work side by side with the mock-up at the same distance and light, settling disputes with void-ratio and colour measurements in an inspection frame. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：樣板牆要在正式澆置前完成並核定，列為開工停檢點，且在工程期間保留在現場作為比對基準；契約中寫明驗收距離、光線條件、檢查框方法與可接受的修補範圍。","observationEn":"Site practice: Complete and approve the mock-up before production casting as a hold point, keep it on site throughout the job as the reference, and write viewing distance, lighting, inspection-frame method and acceptable repair scope into the contract.","failure":"注意干擾：樣板牆只做一片光滑小面，沒有拼縫、繫桿孔或施工縫，正式工程出現的問題在樣板上從未被驗證；未約定觀看距離，業主以手電筒貼近檢查每一個小孔，導致無止境的修補要求。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A mock-up that is only a small smooth panel without joints, tie holes or construction joints never tests the problems that appear on the real work; with no agreed viewing distance, the owner inspects every pinhole with a torch at close range and repair demands never end. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"樣板牆完成後由業主、建築師、結構工程師與承包商在規定距離與自然光下共同檢視並書面核定，拍照存檔；正式工程驗收時在相同距離與光線下與樣板牆並列比較，爭議部分以檢查框量測孔洞比例與色差。","textEn":"Once the mock-up is complete, owner, architect, structural engineer and contractor inspect it together at the specified distance in daylight, approve it in writing and photograph it; at acceptance compare the work side by side with the mock-up at the same distance and light, settling disputes with void-ratio and colour measurements in an inspection frame.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"樣板牆要在正式澆置前完成並核定，列為開工停檢點，且在工程期間保留在現場作為比對基準；契約中寫明驗收距離、光線條件、檢查框方法與可接受的修補範圍。","textEn":"Complete and approve the mock-up before production casting as a hold point, keep it on site throughout the job as the reference, and write viewing distance, lighting, inspection-frame method and acceptable repair scope into the contract.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樣板牆、比對基準與驗收距離」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mock-up, reference standard and viewing distance\"?","options":["樣板牆完成後由業主、建築師、結構工程師與承包商在規定距離與自然光下共同檢視並書面核定，拍照存檔。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要強度等級相同，不同預拌廠的混凝土在外觀上沒有差別。"],"optionsEn":["Once the mock-up is complete, owner, architect, structural engineer and contractor inspect it together at the specified distance in daylight, approve it in writing and photograph it.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","If the strength grade is the same, concrete from different plants looks the same."],"answer":0,"explanation":"樣板牆完成後由業主、建築師、結構工程師與承包商在規定距離與自然光下共同檢視並書面核定，拍照存檔；正式工程驗收時在相同距離與光線下與樣板牆並列比較，爭議部分以檢查框量測孔洞比例與色差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Once the mock-up is complete, owner, architect, structural engineer and contractor inspect it together at the specified distance in daylight, approve it in writing and photograph it; at acceptance compare the work side by side with the mock-up at the same distance and light, settling disputes with void-ratio and colour measurements in an inspection frame. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b095-v13-28","title":"樣板牆、比對基準與驗收距離：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mock-up, reference standard and viewing distance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樣板牆與觀看距離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mock-up and viewing distance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"樣板牆只做一片光滑小面，沒有拼縫、繫桿孔或施工縫，正式工程出現的問題在樣板上從未被驗證；未約定觀看距離，業主以手電筒貼近檢查每一個小孔，導致無止境的修補要求。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A mock-up that is only a small smooth panel without joints, tie holes or construction joints never tests the problems that appear on the real work; with no agreed viewing distance, the owner inspects every pinhole with a torch at close range and repair demands never end. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：驗收時還必須規定觀看距離與光線條件：同一面牆在 1 m 與 10 m 外看，可接受的缺陷完全不同。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Acceptance must also state viewing distance and light: the same wall seen from 1 m and from 10 m tolerates entirely different defects.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「樣板牆只是給業主看的展示品，正式施工時不需要再參照。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The mock-up is just a showpiece for the owner and need not be referred to during construction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"樣板牆只做一片光滑小面，沒有拼縫、繫桿孔或施工縫，正式工程出現的問題在樣板上從未被驗證；未約定觀看距離，業主以手電筒貼近檢查每一個小孔，導致無止境的修補要求。","textEn":"A mock-up that is only a small smooth panel without joints, tie holes or construction joints never tests the problems that appear on the real work; with no agreed viewing distance, the owner inspects every pinhole with a torch at close range and repair demands never end.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樣板牆、比對基準與驗收距離」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mock-up, reference standard and viewing distance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","樣板牆只做一片光滑小面，沒有拼縫、繫桿孔或施工縫，正式工程出現的問題在樣板上從未被驗證；未約定觀看距離，業主以手電筒貼近檢查每一個小孔，導致無止境的修補要求。","清水混凝土的外觀好壞只能靠主觀感覺判斷，無法量測。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","A mock-up that is only a small smooth panel without joints, tie holes or construction joints never tests the problems that appear on the real work.","The appearance of exposed concrete can only be judged subjectively and cannot be measured."],"answer":1,"explanation":"樣板牆只做一片光滑小面，沒有拼縫、繫桿孔或施工縫，正式工程出現的問題在樣板上從未被驗證；未約定觀看距離，業主以手電筒貼近檢查每一個小孔，導致無止境的修補要求。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A mock-up that is only a small smooth panel without joints, tie holes or construction joints never tests the problems that appear on the real work; with no agreed viewing distance, the owner inspects every pinhole with a torch at close range and repair demands never end. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b095-v13-29","title":"色差、平整度與孔洞的量化檢測：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Quantifying colour, flatness and voids: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「表面亮度與色差量測」如何影響清水混凝土模板與澆置的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Surface lightness and colour measurement” governs force, deformation or durability in “Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"清水混凝土的驗收若只靠主觀印象，很容易產生爭議，因此應盡量把外觀指標量化：以色差儀或標準灰卡量測表面明度與色差，以直尺或數位平整度儀量測平整度，以檢查框與影像分析量測孔洞比例。量測要在混凝土乾燥程度相近時進行，因為潮濕表面顏色較深；同一面牆的量測點應涵蓋不同澆置批次與樓層，才能看出系統性的變化。這些數據也能回饋到施工，例如發現下層顏色偏深時檢討振搗與漿體上浮。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「表面亮度與色差量測」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Acceptance by subjective impression alone invites disputes, so appearance criteria should be quantified where possible: measure surface lightness and colour difference with a colorimeter or standard grey cards, flatness with a straightedge or digital flatness gauge, and void ratio with an inspection frame and image analysis. Measure when the concrete is similarly dry, because damp surfaces look darker, and spread points on each wall across different batches and storeys to reveal systematic changes. The data also feed back into construction; for example, a darker lower zone prompts a review of vibration and paste flotation. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Surface lightness and colour measurement” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以 L*（明度）比較：樣板牆平均 L* = 65.0，某面牆平均 62.0，ΔL* = 3.0，超過假設容許值 ±2.0，需檢討原因；若同一面牆內最高與最低區塊相差 ΔL* = 1.2，則屬可接受的自然變化。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Compare lightness L*: the mock-up averages L* = 65.0 and a wall averages 62.0, ΔL* = 3.0, beyond an assumed tolerance of ±2.0, so the cause must be investigated; a spread of ΔL* = 1.2 between the lightest and darkest zones within one wall counts as acceptable natural variation.","failure":"常見誤解：「清水混凝土的外觀好壞只能靠主觀感覺判斷，無法量測。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The appearance of exposed concrete can only be judged subjectively and cannot be measured.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「表面亮度與色差量測」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Surface lightness and colour measurement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-29-k1","title":"色差、平整度與孔洞的量化檢測","titleEn":"Quantifying colour, flatness and voids","text":"清水混凝土的驗收若只靠主觀印象，很容易產生爭議，因此應盡量把外觀指標量化：以色差儀或標準灰卡量測表面明度與色差，以直尺或數位平整度儀量測平整度，以檢查框與影像分析量測孔洞比例。量測要在混凝土乾燥程度相近時進行，因為潮濕表面顏色較深；同一面牆的量測點應涵蓋不同澆置批次與樓層，才能看出系統性的變化。","textEn":"Acceptance by subjective impression alone invites disputes, so appearance criteria should be quantified where possible: measure surface lightness and colour difference with a colorimeter or standard grey cards, flatness with a straightedge or digital flatness gauge, and void ratio with an inspection frame and image analysis. Measure when the concrete is similarly dry, because damp surfaces look darker, and spread points on each wall across different batches and storeys to reveal systematic changes.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：清水混凝土的外觀好壞只能靠主觀感覺判斷，無法量測。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The appearance of exposed concrete can only be judged subjectively and cannot be measured. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「色差、平整度與孔洞的量化檢測」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Quantifying colour, flatness and voids\" is correct?","options":["清水混凝土的外觀好壞只能靠主觀感覺判斷，無法量測。","清水混凝土很耐久，不需要任何表面保護與修補計畫。","清水混凝土的驗收若只靠主觀印象，很容易產生爭議，因此應盡量把外觀指標量化：以色差儀或標準灰卡量測表面明度與色差，以直尺或數位平整度儀量測平整度，以檢查框與影像分析量測孔洞比例。"],"optionsEn":["The appearance of exposed concrete can only be judged subjectively and cannot be measured.","Exposed concrete is durable and needs no surface protection or repair plan.","Acceptance by subjective impression alone invites disputes, so appearance criteria should be quantified where possible: measure surface lightness and colour difference with a colorimeter or standard grey cards, flatness with a straightedge or digital flatness gauge, and void ratio with an inspection frame and image analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"清水混凝土的驗收若只靠主觀印象，很容易產生爭議，因此應盡量把外觀指標量化：以色差儀或標準灰卡量測表面明度與色差，以直尺或數位平整度儀量測平整度，以檢查框與影像分析量測孔洞比例。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Acceptance by subjective impression alone invites disputes, so appearance criteria should be quantified where possible: measure surface lightness and colour difference with a colorimeter or standard grey cards, flatness with a straightedge or digital flatness gauge, and void ratio with an inspection frame and image analysis. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b095-v13-30","title":"色差、平整度與孔洞的量化檢測：定量估算","titleEn":"Quantifying colour, flatness and voids: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「表面亮度與色差量測」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Surface lightness and colour measurement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以 L*（明度）比較：樣板牆平均 L* = 65.0，某面牆平均 62.0，ΔL* = 3.0，超過假設容許值 ±2.0，需檢討原因；若同一面牆內最高與最低區塊相差 ΔL* = 1.2，則屬可接受的自然變化。平整度：3 m 直尺下最大間隙 3 mm，相當於 1/1,000。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Compare lightness L*: the mock-up averages L* = 65.0 and a wall averages 62.0, ΔL* = 3.0, beyond an assumed tolerance of ±2.0, so the cause must be investigated; a spread of ΔL* = 1.2 between the lightest and darkest zones within one wall counts as acceptable natural variation. Flatness: a maximum gap of 3 mm under a 3 m straightedge is 1/1,000. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測計畫規定儀器、校正方式、量測時機（例如拆模後 28 天、表面乾燥）、點位密度與紀錄格式；同一儀器與操作者量測樣板牆與正式牆體，結果以面板編號與澆置批次整理。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The measurement plan specifies instruments, calibration, timing (for example 28 days after stripping with a dry surface), point density and record format; measure mock-up and production walls with the same instrument and operator and organise results by panel number and pour batch.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以 L*（明度）比較：樣板牆平均 L* = 65.0，某面牆平均 62.0，ΔL* = 3.0，超過假設容許值 ±2.0，需檢討原因；若同一面牆內最高與最低區塊相差 ΔL* = 1.2，則屬可接受的自然變化。平整度：3 m 直尺下最大間隙 3 mm，相當於 1/1,000。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Compare lightness L*: the mock-up averages L* = 65.0 and a wall averages 62.0, ΔL* = 3.0, beyond an assumed tolerance of ±2.0, so the cause must be investigated; a spread of ΔL* = 1.2 between the lightest and darkest zones within one wall counts as acceptable natural variation. Flatness: a maximum gap of 3 mm under a 3 m straightedge is 1/1,000. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「色差、平整度與孔洞的量化檢測」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Quantifying colour, flatness and voids\", which statement holds?","options":["以 L*（明度）比較：樣板牆平均 L* = 65.0，某面牆平均 62.0，ΔL* = 3.0，超過假設容許值 ±2.0，需檢討原因。","清水混凝土就是不粉刷的普通混凝土，不需要特別的規格。","脫模劑塗得越多越好，可以保證拆模後表面光滑。"],"optionsEn":["Compare lightness L*: the mock-up averages L* = 65.0 and a wall averages 62.0, ΔL* = 3.0, beyond an assumed tolerance of ±2.0, so the cause must be investigated.","Exposed concrete is just ordinary concrete left unpainted and needs no special specification.","The more release agent the better; it guarantees a smooth surface after stripping."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以 L*（明度）比較：樣板牆平均 L* = 65.0，某面牆平均 62.0，ΔL* = 3.0，超過假設容許值 ±2.0，需檢討原因；若同一面牆內最高與最低區塊相差 ΔL* = 1.2，則屬可接受的自然變化。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Compare lightness L*: the mock-up averages L* = 65.0 and a wall averages 62.0, ΔL* = 3.0, beyond an assumed tolerance of ±2.0, so the cause must be investigated; a spread of ΔL* = 1.2 between the lightest and darkest zones within one wall counts as acceptable natural variation. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b095-v13-31","title":"色差、平整度與孔洞的量化檢測：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Quantifying colour, flatness and voids: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「表面亮度與色差量測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Surface lightness and colour measurement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測計畫規定儀器、校正方式、量測時機（例如拆模後 28 天、表面乾燥）、點位密度與紀錄格式；同一儀器與操作者量測樣板牆與正式牆體，結果以面板編號與澆置批次整理。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The measurement plan specifies instruments, calibration, timing (for example 28 days after stripping with a dry surface), point density and record format; measure mock-up and production walls with the same instrument and operator and organise results by panel number and pour batch. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在契約中明訂外觀量測方法、時機與允收值，並約定量測不合格時的處理順序：先比對樣板、再評估是否為可接受的自然變化、最後才決定修補；修補方法本身也要先在樣板牆上試做。","observationEn":"Site practice: Specify appearance measurement methods, timing and acceptance values in the contract and agree the sequence for failures: compare with the mock-up, assess whether it is acceptable natural variation, and only then decide on repair, with any repair method trialled first on the mock-up.","failure":"注意干擾：拆模後第二天就在潮濕表面量色差，數據與日後乾燥後完全不同，據此要求的修補反而造成新的色斑；量測點只選在明顯缺陷處，無法代表整面牆，引發不必要的整面處理。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Measuring colour on a damp surface the day after stripping gives data unlike the dry surface later, and repairs ordered on that basis create new blotches; choosing points only at obvious defects does not represent the wall and triggers unnecessary whole-face treatment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測計畫規定儀器、校正方式、量測時機（例如拆模後 28 天、表面乾燥）、點位密度與紀錄格式；同一儀器與操作者量測樣板牆與正式牆體，結果以面板編號與澆置批次整理。","textEn":"The measurement plan specifies instruments, calibration, timing (for example 28 days after stripping with a dry surface), point density and record format; measure mock-up and production walls with the same instrument and operator and organise results by panel number and pour batch.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在契約中明訂外觀量測方法、時機與允收值，並約定量測不合格時的處理順序：先比對樣板、再評估是否為可接受的自然變化、最後才決定修補；修補方法本身也要先在樣板牆上試做。","textEn":"Specify appearance measurement methods, timing and acceptance values in the contract and agree the sequence for failures: compare with the mock-up, assess whether it is acceptable natural variation, and only then decide on repair, with any repair method trialled first on the mock-up.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「色差、平整度與孔洞的量化檢測」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Quantifying colour, flatness and voids\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","量測計畫規定儀器、校正方式、量測時機（例如拆模後 28 天、表面乾燥）、點位密度與紀錄格式；同一儀器與操作者量測樣板牆與正式牆體，結果以面板編號與澆置批次整理。","清水模板只要表面光滑就好，背楞間距照一般結構模板即可。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","The measurement plan specifies instruments, calibration, timing (for example 28 days after stripping with a dry surface), point density and record format.","Exposed-concrete forms only need a smooth facing; stud spacing can follow ordinary structural forms."],"answer":1,"explanation":"量測計畫規定儀器、校正方式、量測時機（例如拆模後 28 天、表面乾燥）、點位密度與紀錄格式；同一儀器與操作者量測樣板牆與正式牆體，結果以面板編號與澆置批次整理。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The measurement plan specifies instruments, calibration, timing (for example 28 days after stripping with a dry surface), point density and record format; measure mock-up and production walls with the same instrument and operator and organise results by panel number and pour batch. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b095-v13-32","title":"色差、平整度與孔洞的量化檢測：失效診斷","titleEn":"Quantifying colour, flatness and voids: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「表面亮度與色差量測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Surface lightness and colour measurement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"拆模後第二天就在潮濕表面量色差，數據與日後乾燥後完全不同，據此要求的修補反而造成新的色斑；量測點只選在明顯缺陷處，無法代表整面牆，引發不必要的整面處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Measuring colour on a damp surface the day after stripping gives data unlike the dry surface later, and repairs ordered on that basis create new blotches; choosing points only at obvious defects does not represent the wall and triggers unnecessary whole-face treatment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這些數據也能回饋到施工，例如發現下層顏色偏深時檢討振搗與漿體上浮。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The data also feed back into construction; for example, a darker lower zone prompts a review of vibration and paste flotation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「清水混凝土的外觀好壞只能靠主觀感覺判斷，無法量測。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The appearance of exposed concrete can only be judged subjectively and cannot be measured.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"拆模後第二天就在潮濕表面量色差，數據與日後乾燥後完全不同，據此要求的修補反而造成新的色斑；量測點只選在明顯缺陷處，無法代表整面牆，引發不必要的整面處理。","textEn":"Measuring colour on a damp surface the day after stripping gives data unlike the dry surface later, and repairs ordered on that basis create new blotches; choosing points only at obvious defects does not represent the wall and triggers unnecessary whole-face treatment.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「色差、平整度與孔洞的量化檢測」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Quantifying colour, flatness and voids\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","清水混凝土很耐久，不需要任何表面保護與修補計畫。","拆模後第二天就在潮濕表面量色差，數據與日後乾燥後完全不同，據此要求的修補反而造成新的色斑；量測點只選在明顯缺陷處，無法代表整面牆，引發不必要的整面處理。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Exposed concrete is durable and needs no surface protection or repair plan.","Measuring colour on a damp surface the day after stripping gives data unlike the dry surface later, and repairs ordered on that basis create new blotches."],"answer":2,"explanation":"拆模後第二天就在潮濕表面量色差，數據與日後乾燥後完全不同，據此要求的修補反而造成新的色斑；量測點只選在明顯缺陷處，無法代表整面牆，引發不必要的整面處理。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Measuring colour on a damp surface the day after stripping gives data unlike the dry surface later, and repairs ordered on that basis create new blotches; choosing points only at obvious defects does not represent the wall and triggers unnecessary whole-face treatment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b095-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「表面保護、污染與修補」與「清潔、修補樣本與長期外觀管理」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Surface protection, soiling and repair\" and \"Cleaning, repair samples and long-term appearance\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b095-v13-33","title":"表面保護、污染與修補：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Surface protection, soiling and repair: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「撥水保護與修補」如何影響清水混凝土模板與澆置的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Water-repellent protection and repair” governs force, deformation or durability in “Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"清水混凝土沒有塗裝保護，表面毛細孔會吸水，雨水帶著灰塵與微生物進入表層，形成流痕與黑斑；吸水也會加速凍融、碳化與鋼筋鏽蝕。常見作法是在完工後施作滲透型撥水劑（如矽烷或矽氧烷），降低表面吸水但不改變外觀與透氣性。修補是清水混凝土最難的工作：修補砂漿必須與周圍顏色、質感一致，而且新舊材料的顏色會隨時間以不同速度變化，所以修補配方要在樣板牆上試驗並放置一段時間觀察。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「撥水保護與修補」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Exposed concrete has no paint, so surface capillaries absorb water and rain carries dust and micro-organisms into the surface layer, forming streaks and dark patches; absorption also accelerates freeze–thaw, carbonation and bar corrosion. A common measure is a penetrating water repellent such as silane or siloxane after completion, reducing absorption without changing appearance or breathability. Repair is the hardest job in exposed concrete: repair mortar must match the surrounding colour and texture, and new and old materials change colour at different rates over time, so repair recipes are trialled on the mock-up and left to weather before use. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Water-repellent protection and repair” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：毛細吸水量 W = w·√t。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Capillary uptake W = w·√t.","failure":"常見誤解：「清水混凝土很耐久，不需要任何表面保護與修補計畫。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Exposed concrete is durable and needs no surface protection or repair plan.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「撥水保護與修補」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Water-repellent protection and repair”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-33-k1","title":"表面保護、污染與修補","titleEn":"Surface protection, soiling and repair","text":"清水混凝土沒有塗裝保護，表面毛細孔會吸水，雨水帶著灰塵與微生物進入表層，形成流痕與黑斑；吸水也會加速凍融、碳化與鋼筋鏽蝕。常見作法是在完工後施作滲透型撥水劑（如矽烷或矽氧烷），降低表面吸水但不改變外觀與透氣性。","textEn":"Exposed concrete has no paint, so surface capillaries absorb water and rain carries dust and micro-organisms into the surface layer, forming streaks and dark patches; absorption also accelerates freeze–thaw, carbonation and bar corrosion. A common measure is a penetrating water repellent such as silane or siloxane after completion, reducing absorption without changing appearance or breathability.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：清水混凝土很耐久，不需要任何表面保護與修補計畫。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Exposed concrete is durable and needs no surface protection or repair plan. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「表面保護、污染與修補」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Surface protection, soiling and repair\" is correct?","options":["清水混凝土沒有塗裝保護，表面毛細孔會吸水，雨水帶著灰塵與微生物進入表層，形成流痕與黑斑；吸水也會加速凍融、碳化與鋼筋鏽蝕。","清水混凝土很耐久，不需要任何表面保護與修補計畫。","清水混凝土弄髒了用高壓水柱沖洗就能恢復原貌。"],"optionsEn":["Exposed concrete has no paint, so surface capillaries absorb water and rain carries dust and micro-organisms into the surface layer, forming streaks and dark patches.","Exposed concrete is durable and needs no surface protection or repair plan.","Dirty exposed concrete can be restored to its original look by pressure washing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"清水混凝土沒有塗裝保護，表面毛細孔會吸水，雨水帶著灰塵與微生物進入表層，形成流痕與黑斑；吸水也會加速凍融、碳化與鋼筋鏽蝕。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Exposed concrete has no paint, so surface capillaries absorb water and rain carries dust and micro-organisms into the surface layer, forming streaks and dark patches; absorption also accelerates freeze–thaw, carbonation and bar corrosion. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b095-v13-34","title":"表面保護、污染與修補：定量估算","titleEn":"Surface protection, soiling and repair: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「撥水保護與修補」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Water-repellent protection and repair” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：毛細吸水量 W = w·√t。未處理表面 w = 1.0 kg/m²·h^0.5，4 h 降雨吸水 W = 1.0×√4 = 2.0 kg/m²；以撥水劑降到 w = 0.1 時 W = 0.2 kg/m²，吸水減少 90%，表面污染與凍融風險隨之降低。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Capillary uptake W = w·√t. For an untreated surface with w = 1.0 kg/m²·h^0.5, four hours of rain absorb W = 1.0×√4 = 2.0 kg/m²; a water repellent that cuts w to 0.1 gives W = 0.2 kg/m², a 90% reduction with correspondingly less soiling and freeze–thaw risk. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：撥水劑施作前在樣板牆上試驗外觀是否改變，施作後以卡斯頓管（Karsten tube）或吸水試驗比較處理前後的吸水量；修補配方在樣板牆上試做並至少觀察數週至數月的顏色變化，再核定使用。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before applying a repellent, trial it on the mock-up for any change in appearance, and afterwards compare water uptake before and after with Karsten tubes or absorption tests; trial repair recipes on the mock-up and watch colour change for at least several weeks to months before approval.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"毛細吸水量 W = w·√t。未處理表面 w = 1.0 kg/m²·h^0.5，4 h 降雨吸水 W = 1.0×√4 = 2.0 kg/m²；以撥水劑降到 w = 0.1 時 W = 0.2 kg/m²，吸水減少 90%，表面污染與凍融風險隨之降低。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Capillary uptake W = w·√t. For an untreated surface with w = 1.0 kg/m²·h^0.5, four hours of rain absorb W = 1.0×√4 = 2.0 kg/m²; a water repellent that cuts w to 0.1 gives W = 0.2 kg/m², a 90% reduction with correspondingly less soiling and freeze–thaw risk. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「表面保護、污染與修補」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Surface protection, soiling and repair\", which statement holds?","options":["模板拼縫與繫桿孔只是施工痕跡，交給工地自行安排即可。","毛細吸水量 W = w·√t。","只要強度等級相同，不同預拌廠的混凝土在外觀上沒有差別。"],"optionsEn":["Form joints and tie holes are just construction marks that the site can arrange as it likes.","Capillary uptake W = w·√t.","If the strength grade is the same, concrete from different plants looks the same."],"answer":1,"explanation":"毛細吸水量 W = w·√t。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Capillary uptake W = w·√t. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b095-v13-35","title":"表面保護、污染與修補：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Surface protection, soiling and repair: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「撥水保護與修補」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Water-repellent protection and repair” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"撥水劑施作前在樣板牆上試驗外觀是否改變，施作後以卡斯頓管（Karsten tube）或吸水試驗比較處理前後的吸水量；修補配方在樣板牆上試做並至少觀察數週至數月的顏色變化，再核定使用。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before applying a repellent, trial it on the mock-up for any change in appearance, and afterwards compare water uptake before and after with Karsten tubes or absorption tests; trial repair recipes on the mock-up and watch colour change for at least several weeks to months before approval. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：完工前應決定是否施作撥水劑、產品類型與重塗週期，並在樣板牆上核定；修補程序須規定誰可修補、修補範圍上限、配方與試做，並保存修補位置紀錄供日後維護比對。","observationEn":"Site practice: Decide before completion whether to apply a repellent, which type and how often to recoat, approved on the mock-up; the repair procedure should state who may repair, the maximum repair extent, recipes and trials, and keep a record of repair locations for later maintenance.","failure":"注意干擾：使用成膜型塗料代替滲透型撥水劑，表面變亮且逐年黃化、剝落，清水質感消失；修補砂漿當下顏色相近，一年後明顯偏白或偏深，整面牆布滿補丁。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using a film-forming coating instead of a penetrating repellent makes the surface glossy, yellows and peels over the years and destroys the exposed-concrete texture; repair mortar that matches on the day turns noticeably lighter or darker a year later, leaving the wall covered in patches. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"撥水劑施作前在樣板牆上試驗外觀是否改變，施作後以卡斯頓管（Karsten tube）或吸水試驗比較處理前後的吸水量；修補配方在樣板牆上試做並至少觀察數週至數月的顏色變化，再核定使用。","textEn":"Before applying a repellent, trial it on the mock-up for any change in appearance, and afterwards compare water uptake before and after with Karsten tubes or absorption tests; trial repair recipes on the mock-up and watch colour change for at least several weeks to months before approval.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"完工前應決定是否施作撥水劑、產品類型與重塗週期，並在樣板牆上核定；修補程序須規定誰可修補、修補範圍上限、配方與試做，並保存修補位置紀錄供日後維護比對。","textEn":"Decide before completion whether to apply a repellent, which type and how often to recoat, approved on the mock-up; the repair procedure should state who may repair, the maximum repair extent, recipes and trials, and keep a record of repair locations for later maintenance.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「表面保護、污染與修補」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Surface protection, soiling and repair\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","清水混凝土澆得越快越連續，表面就越均勻。","撥水劑施作前在樣板牆上試驗外觀是否改變，施作後以卡斯頓管（Karsten tube）或吸水試驗比較處理前後的吸水量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The faster and more continuously exposed concrete is placed, the more uniform the surface.","Before applying a repellent, trial it on the mock-up for any change in appearance, and afterwards compare water uptake before and after with Karsten tubes or absorption tests."],"answer":2,"explanation":"撥水劑施作前在樣板牆上試驗外觀是否改變，施作後以卡斯頓管（Karsten tube）或吸水試驗比較處理前後的吸水量；修補配方在樣板牆上試做並至少觀察數週至數月的顏色變化，再核定使用。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before applying a repellent, trial it on the mock-up for any change in appearance, and afterwards compare water uptake before and after with Karsten tubes or absorption tests; trial repair recipes on the mock-up and watch colour change for at least several weeks to months before approval. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b095-v13-36","title":"表面保護、污染與修補：失效診斷","titleEn":"Surface protection, soiling and repair: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「撥水保護與修補」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Water-repellent protection and repair” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"使用成膜型塗料代替滲透型撥水劑，表面變亮且逐年黃化、剝落，清水質感消失；修補砂漿當下顏色相近，一年後明顯偏白或偏深，整面牆布滿補丁。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using a film-forming coating instead of a penetrating repellent makes the surface glossy, yellows and peels over the years and destroys the exposed-concrete texture; repair mortar that matches on the day turns noticeably lighter or darker a year later, leaving the wall covered in patches. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：修補是清水混凝土最難的工作：修補砂漿必須與周圍顏色、質感一致，而且新舊材料的顏色會隨時間以不同速度變化，所以修補配方要在樣板牆上試驗並放置一段時間觀察。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Repair is the hardest job in exposed concrete: repair mortar must match the surrounding colour and texture, and new and old materials change colour at different rates over time, so repair recipes are trialled on the mock-up and left to weather before use.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「清水混凝土很耐久，不需要任何表面保護與修補計畫。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Exposed concrete is durable and needs no surface protection or repair plan.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"使用成膜型塗料代替滲透型撥水劑，表面變亮且逐年黃化、剝落，清水質感消失；修補砂漿當下顏色相近，一年後明顯偏白或偏深，整面牆布滿補丁。","textEn":"Using a film-forming coating instead of a penetrating repellent makes the surface glossy, yellows and peels over the years and destroys the exposed-concrete texture; repair mortar that matches on the day turns noticeably lighter or darker a year later, leaving the wall covered in patches.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「表面保護、污染與修補」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Surface protection, soiling and repair\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["使用成膜型塗料代替滲透型撥水劑，表面變亮且逐年黃化、剝落，清水質感消失；修補砂漿當下顏色相近，一年後明顯偏白或偏深，整面牆布滿補丁。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","清水混凝土弄髒了用高壓水柱沖洗就能恢復原貌。"],"optionsEn":["Using a film-forming coating instead of a penetrating repellent makes the surface glossy, yellows and peels over the years and destroys the exposed-concrete texture.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Dirty exposed concrete can be restored to its original look by pressure washing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"使用成膜型塗料代替滲透型撥水劑，表面變亮且逐年黃化、剝落，清水質感消失；修補砂漿當下顏色相近，一年後明顯偏白或偏深，整面牆布滿補丁。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using a film-forming coating instead of a penetrating repellent makes the surface glossy, yellows and peels over the years and destroys the exposed-concrete texture; repair mortar that matches on the day turns noticeably lighter or darker a year later, leaving the wall covered in patches. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b095-v13-37","title":"清潔、修補樣本與長期外觀管理：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cleaning, repair samples and long-term appearance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「維護手冊與修補樣本」如何影響清水混凝土模板與澆置的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Maintenance manual and repair samples” governs force, deformation or durability in “Architectural exposed-concrete formwork and casting”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"清水混凝土的外觀會隨時間演變：表面碳化使顏色略變，雨水流路形成污痕，綠藻在背陽面生長，繫桿孔塞頭可能鬆脫。沙克研究所於 1991 年被指定為歷史地標，其混凝土與柚木的保存工作顯示，清水建築的維護需要了解原始材料與工法。交接時應移交原配比、面材與脫模劑資料、撥水劑產品與施作紀錄、修補配方與樣本、樣板牆照片與量測基準，並規定可接受的清潔方法；高壓水柱或酸洗會改變表面質感，必須先試驗。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「維護手冊與修補樣本」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Exposed concrete changes with time: surface carbonation shifts colour slightly, rain paths form streaks, algae grow on shaded faces and tie-hole plugs may loosen. The Salk Institute, designated a historic landmark in 1991, shows through its concrete and teak conservation work that maintaining exposed buildings requires knowing the original materials and methods. Handover should deliver the original mix, facing and release-agent data, water-repellent product and application records, repair recipes and samples, mock-up photographs and measurement baselines, and specify acceptable cleaning methods; high-pressure water or acid washing changes surface texture and must be trialled first. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Maintenance manual and repair samples” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：撥水劑用量 0.3 L/m²，清水面 2,400 m² 每次約 2,400×0.3 = 720 L；若每 12 年重塗一次，50 年內約 4 次，共約 2,880 L。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: At 0.3 L/m², 2,400 m² of exposed surface needs about 2,400×0.3 = 720 L per application; recoating every 12 years means about 4 applications and 2,880 L over 50 years.","failure":"常見誤解：「清水混凝土弄髒了用高壓水柱沖洗就能恢復原貌。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Dirty exposed concrete can be restored to its original look by pressure washing.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「維護手冊與修補樣本」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Maintenance manual and repair samples”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-37-k1","title":"清潔、修補樣本與長期外觀管理","titleEn":"Cleaning, repair samples and long-term appearance","text":"清水混凝土的外觀會隨時間演變：表面碳化使顏色略變，雨水流路形成污痕，綠藻在背陽面生長，繫桿孔塞頭可能鬆脫。沙克研究所於 1991 年被指定為歷史地標，其混凝土與柚木的保存工作顯示，清水建築的維護需要了解原始材料與工法。","textEn":"Exposed concrete changes with time: surface carbonation shifts colour slightly, rain paths form streaks, algae grow on shaded faces and tie-hole plugs may loosen. The Salk Institute, designated a historic landmark in 1991, shows through its concrete and teak conservation work that maintaining exposed buildings requires knowing the original materials and methods.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：清水混凝土弄髒了用高壓水柱沖洗就能恢復原貌。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Dirty exposed concrete can be restored to its original look by pressure washing. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「清潔、修補樣本與長期外觀管理」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cleaning, repair samples and long-term appearance\" is correct?","options":["清水混凝土弄髒了用高壓水柱沖洗就能恢復原貌。","清水混凝土的外觀會隨時間演變：表面碳化使顏色略變，雨水流路形成污痕，綠藻在背陽面生長，繫桿孔塞頭可能鬆脫。","清水混凝土就是不粉刷的普通混凝土，不需要特別的規格。"],"optionsEn":["Dirty exposed concrete can be restored to its original look by pressure washing.","Exposed concrete changes with time: surface carbonation shifts colour slightly, rain paths form streaks, algae grow on shaded faces and tie-hole plugs may loosen.","Exposed concrete is just ordinary concrete left unpainted and needs no special specification."],"answer":1,"explanation":"清水混凝土的外觀會隨時間演變：表面碳化使顏色略變，雨水流路形成污痕，綠藻在背陽面生長，繫桿孔塞頭可能鬆脫。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Exposed concrete changes with time: surface carbonation shifts colour slightly, rain paths form streaks, algae grow on shaded faces and tie-hole plugs may loosen. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b095-v13-38","title":"清潔、修補樣本與長期外觀管理：定量估算","titleEn":"Cleaning, repair samples and long-term appearance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「維護手冊與修補樣本」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Maintenance manual and repair samples” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：撥水劑用量 0.3 L/m²，清水面 2,400 m² 每次約 2,400×0.3 = 720 L；若每 12 年重塗一次，50 年內約 4 次，共約 2,880 L。把用量、施作日期與吸水試驗結果列入維護資料庫，可判斷實際重塗時機是否需要提前。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: At 0.3 L/m², 2,400 m² of exposed surface needs about 2,400×0.3 = 720 L per application; recoating every 12 years means about 4 applications and 2,880 L over 50 years. Recording quantities, dates and absorption-test results in a maintenance database shows whether recoating should come sooner. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：維護計畫規定定期目視檢查（污痕、藻類、裂縫、塞頭）、吸水試驗與色差量測，並與交接時的基準照片與數據比較；任何清潔或修補在不顯眼位置先試做，經建築師或維護顧問核可後才施作。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The maintenance plan sets periodic visual inspections for streaks, algae, cracks and plugs, absorption tests and colour measurements, compared with handover baseline photographs and data; trial any cleaning or repair in an inconspicuous spot and proceed only with approval from the architect or a conservation adviser.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"撥水劑用量 0.3 L/m²，清水面 2,400 m² 每次約 2,400×0.3 = 720 L；若每 12 年重塗一次，50 年內約 4 次，共約 2,880 L。把用量、施作日期與吸水試驗結果列入維護資料庫，可判斷實際重塗時機是否需要提前。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"At 0.3 L/m², 2,400 m² of exposed surface needs about 2,400×0.3 = 720 L per application; recoating every 12 years means about 4 applications and 2,880 L over 50 years. Recording quantities, dates and absorption-test results in a maintenance database shows whether recoating should come sooner. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「清潔、修補樣本與長期外觀管理」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cleaning, repair samples and long-term appearance\", which statement holds?","options":["脫模劑塗得越多越好，可以保證拆模後表面光滑。","清水模板只要表面光滑就好，背楞間距照一般結構模板即可。","撥水劑用量 0.3 L/m²，清水面 2,400 m² 每次約 2,400×0.3 = 720 L。"],"optionsEn":["The more release agent the better; it guarantees a smooth surface after stripping.","Exposed-concrete forms only need a smooth facing; stud spacing can follow ordinary structural forms.","At 0.3 L/m², 2,400 m² of exposed surface needs about 2,400×0.3 = 720 L per application."],"answer":2,"explanation":"撥水劑用量 0.3 L/m²，清水面 2,400 m² 每次約 2,400×0.3 = 720 L；若每 12 年重塗一次，50 年內約 4 次，共約 2,880 L。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"At 0.3 L/m², 2,400 m² of exposed surface needs about 2,400×0.3 = 720 L per application; recoating every 12 years means about 4 applications and 2,880 L over 50 years. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b095-v13-39","title":"清潔、修補樣本與長期外觀管理：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cleaning, repair samples and long-term appearance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「維護手冊與修補樣本」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Maintenance manual and repair samples” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"維護計畫規定定期目視檢查（污痕、藻類、裂縫、塞頭）、吸水試驗與色差量測，並與交接時的基準照片與數據比較；任何清潔或修補在不顯眼位置先試做，經建築師或維護顧問核可後才施作。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The maintenance plan sets periodic visual inspections for streaks, algae, cracks and plugs, absorption tests and colour measurements, compared with handover baseline photographs and data; trial any cleaning or repair in an inconspicuous spot and proceed only with approval from the architect or a conservation adviser. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件應包含清水面位置圖、材料與配比資料、撥水劑與修補紀錄、修補樣本與樣板牆照片、允許與禁止的清潔方法；重大清潔或修補應由熟悉清水混凝土的顧問評估並先試做。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover should include a map of exposed faces, material and mix data, repellent and repair records, repair samples and mock-up photographs, and permitted and prohibited cleaning methods; major cleaning or repair should be assessed by a consultant experienced in exposed concrete and trialled first.","failure":"注意干擾：管理單位為去除污痕以高壓水柱或強酸清洗，表面漿體被沖蝕，骨材外露，與未清洗區形成永久差異；缺少原始配比與修補樣本，後來的修補只能憑感覺調色，越補越明顯。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An owner who removes streaks with high-pressure water or strong acid erodes the surface paste and exposes aggregate, leaving a permanent difference from unwashed areas; without the original mix and repair samples, later repairs are colour-matched by guesswork and become ever more obvious. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"維護計畫規定定期目視檢查（污痕、藻類、裂縫、塞頭）、吸水試驗與色差量測，並與交接時的基準照片與數據比較；任何清潔或修補在不顯眼位置先試做，經建築師或維護顧問核可後才施作。","textEn":"The maintenance plan sets periodic visual inspections for streaks, algae, cracks and plugs, absorption tests and colour measurements, compared with handover baseline photographs and data; trial any cleaning or repair in an inconspicuous spot and proceed only with approval from the architect or a conservation adviser.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件應包含清水面位置圖、材料與配比資料、撥水劑與修補紀錄、修補樣本與樣板牆照片、允許與禁止的清潔方法；重大清潔或修補應由熟悉清水混凝土的顧問評估並先試做。","textEn":"Handover should include a map of exposed faces, material and mix data, repellent and repair records, repair samples and mock-up photographs, and permitted and prohibited cleaning methods; major cleaning or repair should be assessed by a consultant experienced in exposed concrete and trialled first.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「清潔、修補樣本與長期外觀管理」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cleaning, repair samples and long-term appearance\"?","options":["維護計畫規定定期目視檢查（污痕、藻類、裂縫、塞頭）、吸水試驗與色差量測，並與交接時的基準照片與數據比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","樣板牆只是給業主看的展示品，正式施工時不需要再參照。"],"optionsEn":["The maintenance plan sets periodic visual inspections for streaks, algae, cracks and plugs, absorption tests and colour measurements, compared with handover baseline photographs and data.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The mock-up is just a showpiece for the owner and need not be referred to during construction."],"answer":0,"explanation":"維護計畫規定定期目視檢查（污痕、藻類、裂縫、塞頭）、吸水試驗與色差量測，並與交接時的基準照片與數據比較；任何清潔或修補在不顯眼位置先試做，經建築師或維護顧問核可後才施作。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The maintenance plan sets periodic visual inspections for streaks, algae, cracks and plugs, absorption tests and colour measurements, compared with handover baseline photographs and data; trial any cleaning or repair in an inconspicuous spot and proceed only with approval from the architect or a conservation adviser. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b095-v13-40","title":"清潔、修補樣本與長期外觀管理：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cleaning, repair samples and long-term appearance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"prerequisiteIds":["b095-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「維護手冊與修補樣本」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Maintenance manual and repair samples” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"管理單位為去除污痕以高壓水柱或強酸清洗，表面漿體被沖蝕，骨材外露，與未清洗區形成永久差異；缺少原始配比與修補樣本，後來的修補只能憑感覺調色，越補越明顯。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An owner who removes streaks with high-pressure water or strong acid erodes the surface paste and exposes aggregate, leaving a permanent difference from unwashed areas; without the original mix and repair samples, later repairs are colour-matched by guesswork and become ever more obvious. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：交接時應移交原配比、面材與脫模劑資料、撥水劑產品與施作紀錄、修補配方與樣本、樣板牆照片與量測基準，並規定可接受的清潔方法；高壓水柱或酸洗會改變表面質感，必須先試驗。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Handover should deliver the original mix, facing and release-agent data, water-repellent product and application records, repair recipes and samples, mock-up photographs and measurement baselines, and specify acceptable cleaning methods; high-pressure water or acid washing changes surface texture and must be trialled first.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「清水混凝土弄髒了用高壓水柱沖洗就能恢復原貌。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dirty exposed concrete can be restored to its original look by pressure washing.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b095-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"管理單位為去除污痕以高壓水柱或強酸清洗，表面漿體被沖蝕，骨材外露，與未清洗區形成永久差異；缺少原始配比與修補樣本，後來的修補只能憑感覺調色，越補越明顯。","textEn":"An owner who removes streaks with high-pressure water or strong acid erodes the surface paste and exposes aggregate, leaving a permanent difference from unwashed areas; without the original mix and repair samples, later repairs are colour-matched by guesswork and become ever more obvious.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]},{"id":"b095-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「清潔、修補樣本與長期外觀管理」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cleaning, repair samples and long-term appearance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","管理單位為去除污痕以高壓水柱或強酸清洗，表面漿體被沖蝕，骨材外露，與未清洗區形成永久差異；缺少原始配比與修補樣本，後來的修補只能憑感覺調色，越補越明顯。","清水混凝土就是不粉刷的普通混凝土，不需要特別的規格。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","An owner who removes streaks with high-pressure water or strong acid erodes the surface paste and exposes aggregate, leaving a permanent difference from unwashed areas.","Exposed concrete is just ordinary concrete left unpainted and needs no special specification."],"answer":1,"explanation":"管理單位為去除污痕以高壓水柱或強酸清洗，表面漿體被沖蝕，骨材外露，與未清洗區形成永久差異；缺少原始配比與修補樣本，後來的修補只能憑感覺調色，越補越明顯。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An owner who removes streaks with high-pressure water or strong acid erodes the surface paste and exposes aggregate, leaving a permanent difference from unwashed areas; without the original mix and repair samples, later repairs are colour-matched by guesswork and become ever more obvious. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-aci-347-3r-13","v13s-aci-301-20-preview","v13s-salk-history","v13s-ibaraki-kasugaoka-church","v13s-wiki-church-of-the-light"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
